\ cm/cmc.4 - the command model's front end in Forth (863): a script in the draft's syntax
\ (docs/COMMAND-MODEL.md) made into Forth for cm's runtime - the Forth tools/cmc.py makes of it,
\ word for word - so that its size, inside rill2's image, can be set against rill2's language part
\ (Q46). Loaded after cm/rt-cm.4, out.4, ctl.4, lib.4 and pipe.4.
\
\ Two passes over the script's text. The first parses it into a tree kept flat: nodes of three
\ cells - a kind and two cells of its own - in an array; a kind of 1-15 opens a node whose children
\ follow it up to a node of kind 0, and 16 and on are leaves. The second makes each command's Forth
\ from the nodes, as cmc.py's Gen does; where cmc.py looks at a whole list of words, it looks ahead
\ by skipping over nodes. The Forth is made as strings joined by blanks, in a heap of their own.
\ The words a command needs - a block's, a capture's, a loop body's - go to the output as they are
\ made, the script's own commands last, in CM.MAIN; the output is EVALUATEd.

\ ---- memory: areas allocated for each script, by its length - the last script's freed
VARIABLE ND0  VARIABLE NDP  VARIABLE NDE           \ the nodes: start, top, end
VARIABLE TX0  VARIABLE TXP  VARIABLE TXE  VARIABLE TXS   \ the texts read; TXS where the one being read starts
VARIABLE CH0  VARIABLE CHP  VARIABLE CHE           \ the strings made
VARIABLE RH0  VARIABLE RHP  VARIABLE RHE           \ frames, scopes and variables
VARIABLE OU0  VARIABLE OUP  VARIABLE OUE           \ the output
: AREA ( u v-start v-top v-end --- )
  >R >R >R  R@ @ ?DUP IF FREE DROP THEN  DUP ALLOCATE THROW  DUP R> !  DUP R> !  + R> ! ;

\ ---- errors: the line, the message, status 2 - as rill2's own
VARIABLE IN-LINE  VARIABLE LN                      \ the line read; the line of the command being made
\ ---- the files read (890): the script, and each one sourced - its lines a range of their own, the
\ script's 1 to its last, each sourced file's after; a line said as "line 3", or "lib.cm line 3"
VARIABLE SF-T  VARIABLE SF-S  VARIABLE SF-CAP   \ in the heap, grown as files come (891; 31 at most before): the files, each
                   \ [base][lines][name][length][text][the line sourcing it]; the readers below, each [text][length][position][line][file]
VARIABLE SF-N  VARIABLE SF-NEXT                    \ how many; the next line free
VARIABLE SF-BASE  VARIABLE SF-LINE0      \ at the prompt the files read on earlier lines are kept, for their lines (909)
: SF ( i --- addr )   6 * CELLS SF-T @ + ;
: SF$ ( i --- c-addr u )   SF 2 CELLS + DUP @ SWAP CELL+ @ ;
: SF-AT ( n --- i )   \ the sourced file whose lines hold n; 0, the script's
  0 SF-N @ 1 MAX 1 ?DO  OVER I SF @ - DUP 0> SWAP I SF CELL+ @ > 0= AND IF DROP I LEAVE THEN  LOOP NIP ;
: SF-LINE. ( n --- )   DUP SF-AT ?DUP IF  DUP SF$ TYPE BL EMIT  SF @ -  THEN  ." line " R-.N ;
' SF-LINE. IS R-LINE.
: CM-ERR ( c-addr u line --- )   \ the message, then where - as a runtime error says it (907: had been "line 4:" first)
  >R R-ERR> ." cm: " TYPE ."  (" R> SF-LINE. ." )" R-NL -4100 THROW ;
: P-ERR ( c-addr u --- )   IN-LINE @ CM-ERR ;
: G-ERR ( c-addr u --- )   LN @ CM-ERR ;
: TOO-BIG ( --- )   S" cm: the script is too big" R-FAIL ;

\ ---- strings: made at the heap's top, joined - one ending at the top grows where it is
: ROOM ( u --- )   CHP @ + CHE @ > IF TOO-BIG THEN ;
: S| ( c-addr u --- c-addr2 u )   DUP ROOM  >R CHP @ R@ MOVE  CHP @ R@  R> CHP +! ;
: CAT ( c-addr1 u1 c-addr2 u2 --- c-addr u )
  DUP 0= IF 2DROP EXIT THEN  2SWAP DUP 0= IF 2DROP EXIT THEN
  2DUP + CHP @ <> IF S| THEN  2SWAP S| NIP + ;
: ++ ( c-addr1 u1 c-addr2 u2 --- c-addr u )   \ joined by a blank
  DUP 0= IF 2DROP EXIT THEN  2SWAP DUP 0= IF 2DROP EXIT THEN  S"  " CAT 2SWAP CAT ;
: #$ ( n --- c-addr u )   S>D TUCK DABS <# #S ROT SIGN #> S| ;
: #++ ( c-addr u n --- c-addr2 u2 )   #$ ++ ;
: T#++ ( c-addr u n --- c-addr2 u2 )   T# ++ ;   \ a number token after code (926)
: TOP$ ( c-addr u --- c-addr2 u )   2DUP + CHP @ <> IF S| THEN ;   \ at the strings' top: SEQ+'s first acc
: SEQ+ ( acc u r u2 --- acc u' )   \ r after acc, a blank between - acc kept at the strings' top, and
  \ what was made since it ended let go: with ++ each command copied all before it, and a script of
  \ 70 variables was "too big" (891); r moved down over what is let go
  DUP 0= IF 2DROP 2DUP + CHP ! EXIT THEN
  2SWAP DUP IF 2DUP + 1+ ELSE OVER THEN  3 PICK OVER + CHE @ > IF TOO-BIG THEN   ( r u2 acc u dest )
  >R 2SWAP TUCK R@ SWAP MOVE  OVER IF BL R@ 1- C! THEN       \ moved first: r may start where the blank goes
  DUP R> + CHP !  SWAP DUP IF 1+ THEN + ;

\ ---- the tree
0 CONSTANT N-END   1 CONSTANT N-CMD  2 CONSTANT N-WRD  3 CONSTANT N-QU  4 CONSTANT N-VR  5 CONSTANT N-CP
6 CONSTANT N-AR    7 CONSTANT N-LS   8 CONSTANT N-MP   9 CONSTANT N-BK  10 CONSTANT N-SP  11 CONSTANT N-IX
16 CONSTANT N-TX  17 CONSTANT N-NM  18 CONSTANT N-BO  19 CONSTANT N-OP
: N, ( a b kind --- )   NDP @ NDE @ = IF TOO-BIG THEN
  NDP @ !  NDP @ 2 CELLS + !  NDP @ CELL+ !  3 CELLS NDP +! ;
: N) ( --- )   0 0 N-END N, ;
: N+ ( node --- node' )   3 CELLS + ;
: @A ( node --- a )   CELL+ @ ;
: @B ( node --- b )   2 CELLS + @ ;
: NSKIP ( node --- node' )   \ past a node and its children
  0 BEGIN OVER @ DUP 1 16 WITHIN IF DROP 1+ ELSE 0= IF 1- THEN THEN  SWAP N+ SWAP  DUP 0= UNTIL DROP ;
: BARE? ( w --- f )   N+ DUP @ N-TX = SWAP N+ @ 0= AND ;     \ a word that is one text
: BARE$ ( w --- c-addr u )   N+ DUP @A SWAP @B ;
: BARE= ( w c-addr u --- f )   ROT DUP BARE? IF BARE$ COMPARE 0= ELSE DROP 2DROP 0 THEN ;
: BARE-IN? ( node c-addr u --- f )   \ a bare word so anywhere in node's subtree
  >R >R DUP NSKIP SWAP
  BEGIN 2DUP <> WHILE  DUP @ N-WRD = IF DUP R> R> 2DUP >R >R BARE= IF 2DROP R> R> 2DROP -1 EXIT THEN THEN  N+ REPEAT
  2DROP R> R> 2DROP 0 ;

\ ---- reading: the first pass, as cmc.py's parse_ functions
VARIABLE IN-TEXT  VARIABLE IN-LEN  VARIABLE IN-POS           \ the text, its length, where reading is
: PK ( k --- c )   IN-POS @ + DUP IN-LEN @ < IF IN-TEXT @ + C@ ELSE DROP 0 THEN ;   \ the character k ahead; 0 past the end
: CUR ( --- c )   0 PK ;
VARIABLE HD-AT  -1 HD-AT !  VARIABLE HD-TO   \ a line's newline, past which reading jumps over the here-documents read ahead (963)
: HD-JUMP ( --- )   HD-TO @ HD-AT @ 1+ ?DO  IN-TEXT @ I + C@ 10 = IF 1 IN-LINE +! THEN  LOOP  HD-TO @ 1- IN-POS !  -1 HD-AT ! ;
: GET ( --- c )   CUR  DUP 10 = IF 1 IN-LINE +!  IN-POS @ HD-AT @ = IF HD-JUMP THEN THEN  1 IN-POS +! ;
: HERE-IN ( --- c-addr )   IN-TEXT @ IN-POS @ + ;
: BLANK? ( c nl? --- f )   OVER 10 = AND  OVER BL = OR  OVER 9 = OR  SWAP 13 = OR ;
: DIG? ( c --- f )   [CHAR] 0 [CHAR] 9 1+ WITHIN ;
: NAME0? ( c --- f )   DUP [CHAR] _ = SWAP 32 OR [CHAR] a [CHAR] z 1+ WITHIN OR ;
: NAMEC? ( c --- f )   DUP NAME0? SWAP DIG? OR ;
: SKIP-WS ( nl? --- )   \ blanks - and line ends, if nl? - and comments: # at a word's start to the line's end
  BEGIN  BEGIN CUR OVER BLANK? WHILE GET DROP REPEAT
    CUR [CHAR] # <> IF DROP EXIT THEN
    BEGIN CUR DUP 10 <> SWAP 0<> AND WHILE GET DROP REPEAT
  DUP 0= UNTIL DROP ;
: T0 ( --- )   TXP @ TXS ! ;                         \ a text begun, where the texts end
: T, ( c --- )   TXP @ C!  1 TXP +! ;
: T) ( --- )   TXP @ TXS @ - ?DUP IF TXS @ SWAP N-TX N, THEN  T0 ;   \ the text read, a leaf - if any
DEFER CMDS ( close closer --- )   DEFER WORD-P ( closer --- )   DEFER ARITH-P ( --- )
: LETTER? ( c --- f )   32 OR [CHAR] a [CHAR] z 1+ WITHIN ;
: NAME-P ( --- c-addr u )   \ a name's characters - and a - between letters, kebab-case, as a def's name had (930)
  HERE-IN  BEGIN CUR NAMEC?  CUR [CHAR] - = 1 PK LETTER? AND  OR WHILE GET DROP REPEAT  HERE-IN OVER - ;
: KEYS-P ( --- )   \ [key]...: each key a word, then the node's end - a N-VR's or a N-IX's
  BEGIN CUR [CHAR] [ = WHILE  GET DROP 0 SKIP-WS NDP @ [CHAR] ] WORD-P  @B IF S" a : after an index" P-ERR THEN
    0 SKIP-WS  GET [CHAR] ] <> IF S" ] missing after a key" P-ERR THEN  REPEAT  N) ;   \ (975: "k": a map's)
: VAR-P ( --- )   \ name[key]...: a N-VR, its keys words
  NAME-P N-VR N, KEYS-P ;
VARIABLE IN-QU                                     \ reading a "...": ${name} allowed (899)
: DOLLAR-P ( --- )   \ after a $: (( )), ( ), a name - or the $ itself, a text (867: no ${name} - one way)
  CUR [CHAR] ( = IF  1 PK [CHAR] ( = IF GET GET 2DROP ARITH-P EXIT THEN
    GET DROP 0 0 N-CP N,  [CHAR] ) DUP CMDS  N) EXIT THEN
  CUR [CHAR] { = IF  IN-QU @ 0= IF S" ${name} is for a double-quoted text, where a name's letters follow it - $name here" P-ERR THEN
    GET DROP CUR NAME0? 0= IF S" ${ wants a name" P-ERR THEN  VAR-P  GET [CHAR] } <> IF S" } missing after ${name" P-ERR THEN EXIT THEN
  CUR NAME0? IF VAR-P EXIT THEN
  CUR DIG? IF S" $1 is sh's - the script's arguments are $args, $args[0] the first" P-ERR THEN   \ (916)
  CUR [CHAR] ? = IF S" $? is sh's - the last command's status is $status" P-ERR THEN      \ sh's others (974): said
  CUR [CHAR] # = IF S" $# is sh's - $($args count) counts the arguments" P-ERR THEN       \ as $1 is, where they had
  CUR [CHAR] @ = CUR [CHAR] * = OR IF S" $@ and $* are sh's - @args spreads the arguments, $args is their list" P-ERR THEN
  CUR [CHAR] ! = IF S" $! is sh's - $job is the job & started last" P-ERR THEN              \ been "nothing right after"
  S" $" N-TX N, ;
: IX? ( --- )   \ [key]... after a value written in one word - a list or map, a text, a capture, a spread's capture -
  \ a N-IX of its keys, after the value (913): as $name[key] is a variable's, so [a b c][1] and $(cmd)[0]
  CUR [CHAR] [ <> IF EXIT THEN  0 0 N-IX N, KEYS-P ;
VARIABLE IN-HD   CREATE ESC1 1 ALLOT                \ reading a here-document's body; a character for a message
: ESC-ERR ( c --- )   \ a \ before a character that is no escape (970)
  DUP 10 = OVER 13 = OR OVER 0= OR IF DROP S" \ at a line's end" ELSE ESC1 C!  S" \" ESC1 1 CAT THEN
  S"  is no escape in " CAT  IN-HD @ IF S" a here-document" ELSE S" a double-quoted text" THEN CAT
  S" ; \n \t \r are, and \ before \ $ @ [ or a quote - \\ for a backslash, '...' takes all as written" CAT P-ERR ;
: QU-ESC ( --- )   \ a \ and the character after it, in "..." and a here-document: \n a newline, \t a tab, \r a carriage
  1 PK  DUP [CHAR] n = IF DROP 10 ELSE  DUP [CHAR] t = IF DROP 9 ELSE  DUP [CHAR] r = IF DROP 13 ELSE   \ return; \
    DUP [CHAR] " = OVER [CHAR] \ = OR OVER [CHAR] $ = OR OVER [CHAR] @ = OR OVER [CHAR] [ = OR 0= IF ESC-ERR THEN  \ " $ @ [
  THEN THEN THEN  GET DROP GET DROP T, ;   \ the character; any other an error (970: it had been the character, "\d" d)
: QU-DOLLAR ( --- )   GET DROP T) -1 IN-QU ! DOLLAR-P 0 IN-QU ! IX? T0 ;   \ $(cmd)[k] indexed, as in a word
: QU-AT ( c --- )   \ @( ) here would be the characters themselves: written for $( ), three times in 960's round
  [CHAR] @ = IF 1 PK [CHAR] ( = IF S" @( ) is not taken in a double-quoted text or a here-document - $( ) is the text there, \@( the characters" P-ERR THEN THEN ;
: QUOTED-P ( --- )   \ "...": a N-QU of texts - \n, \t, \r, \ before \ " $ @ [ in them (970) - and $s
  IN-HD @ >R  0 IN-HD !  0 0 N-QU N,  T0                 \ one inside a here-document's $( ): its errors its own
  BEGIN CUR DUP [CHAR] " <> WHILE
    DUP 0= IF S" a closing quote is missing" P-ERR THEN
    DUP [CHAR] \ = IF DROP QU-ESC ELSE  DUP [CHAR] $ = IF DROP QU-DOLLAR ELSE  QU-AT GET T,  THEN THEN
  REPEAT DROP GET DROP T) N)  R> IN-HD ! ;
: SQUOTE-P ( --- )   \ after a ': the text to the next ', a leaf - '' too, an empty text
  T0 BEGIN CUR [CHAR] ' <> WHILE CUR 0= IF S" ' missing" P-ERR THEN GET T, REPEAT  GET DROP  TXS @ TXP @ OVER - N-TX N, T0 ;
: OPR, ( n --- )   HERE-IN OVER N-OP N,  0 ?DO GET DROP LOOP ;      \ an operator of n characters, a leaf
: OPR2? ( --- f )   0  12 0 DO  S" ==!=<=>=&&||" DROP I +  DUP C@ CUR =  SWAP 1+ C@ 1 PK =  AND OR  2 +LOOP ;
: ONE-OF? ( c c-addr u --- f )   0 SWAP 0 ?DO  OVER I + C@ 3 PICK = OR  LOOP NIP NIP ;
: A-DIGIT ( n c --- n' )   \ a digit more of a number in $(( )), checked (923): past 64 bits it had wrapped
  [CHAR] 0 -  OVER 922337203685477580 >  2 PICK 922337203685477580 = 2 PICK 7 > AND  OR
  IF S" a number past 64 bits" P-ERR THEN  SWAP 10 * + ;
: ARITH-P' ( --- )   \ (( )): numbers, $values and operators in a N-AR - ended by )) outside any ( )
  IN-LINE @ 0 N-AR N,  0
  BEGIN  BEGIN CUR -1 BLANK? WHILE GET DROP REPEAT
    CUR 0= IF S" )) missing" P-ERR THEN
    CUR [CHAR] ) = OVER 0= AND  1 PK [CHAR] ) = AND IF DROP GET GET 2DROP N) EXIT THEN
    CUR DIG? IF  0 BEGIN CUR DIG? WHILE GET A-DIGIT REPEAT  0 N-NM N,
    ELSE CUR [CHAR] $ = IF GET DROP DOLLAR-P
    ELSE CUR [CHAR] " = IF GET DROP QUOTED-P ELSE CUR [CHAR] ' = IF GET DROP SQUOTE-P     \ texts too (874): $(( $a == "yes" ))
    ELSE OPR2? IF 2 OPR,
    ELSE CUR S" +-*/%<>()!" ONE-OF? IF  CUR [CHAR] ( = IF 1+ THEN  CUR [CHAR] ) = IF 1- THEN  1 OPR,
    ELSE CUR NAME0? IF S" a word in $(( )) - a text there is quoted, a variable has its $" P-ERR THEN   \ (916)
      S" (( )) holds numbers, $values, texts and operators" P-ERR THEN THEN THEN THEN THEN THEN
  AGAIN ;
' ARITH-P' IS ARITH-P
VARIABLE BARE                                      \ the word read so far: plain text, nothing quoted
: WORD-END? ( c closer --- f )   OVER = SWAP  DUP 0= OVER [CHAR] ; = OR  SWAP -1 BLANK? OR  OR ;
: NUM? ( c-addr u --- n f )   \ the text -?[0-9]+: its value and true
  OVER C@ [CHAR] - = >R  R@ IF 1 /STRING THEN  R> ROT ROT
  DUP 0= IF DROP 2DROP 0 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP 18 > IF DROP 2DROP 0 0 EXIT THEN          \ a number as written (915): 01, -0 and 20 digits stay texts -
  OVER C@ [CHAR] 0 = OVER 1 > 3 PICK OR AND IF DROP 2DROP 0 0 EXIT THEN   \ 01 had become 1, 20 digits wrapped
  0 SWAP 0 DO  OVER I + C@ DUP DIG? 0= IF DROP 2DROP DROP 0 0 UNLOOP EXIT THEN  [CHAR] 0 - SWAP 10 * +  LOOP
  NIP SWAP IF NEGATE THEN -1 ;
: LITERAL? ( tx --- )   \ a plain word alone: a number, true or false
  DUP @A OVER @B NUM? IF OVER CELL+ ! N-NM SWAP ! EXIT THEN DROP
  DUP @A OVER @B 2DUP S" true" COMPARE 0= IF 2DROP -1 ELSE S" false" COMPARE IF DROP EXIT THEN 0 THEN
  OVER CELL+ ! N-BO SWAP ! ;
VARIABLE GLOBW                                     \ an unquoted * or ? read in the word: a glob (872; with $s, 881)
: OP= ( c-addr u c-addr2 u2 --- c-addr u f )   2OVER COMPARE 0= ;
: OPERATOR? ( c-addr u --- f )   \ | || && & > >> < << 2> 2>> &> 2>&1 >&2 1>&2
  DUP 1 = IF DROP C@ S" |&><" ONE-OF? EXIT THEN
  S" <<" OP= IF 2DROP -1 EXIT THEN  S" ||" OP= >R  S" &&" OP= >R  S" >>" OP= >R  S" 2>" OP= >R  S" &>" OP= >R  S" 2>>" OP= >R  S" >&2" OP= >R  S" 2>&1" OP= >R
  S" 1>&2" OP=  R> OR R> OR R> OR R> OR R> OR R> OR R> OR R> OR  NIP NIP ;
: GLUED? ( c-addr u --- f )   \ an operator glued to a word, as sh reads it: 2>/dev/null, >out, hi|tr, cmd& (899)
  2DUP OPERATOR? IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  OVER C@ S" |&<>" ONE-OF? IF 2DROP -1 EXIT THEN
  2DUP BEGIN DUP WHILE OVER C@ DIG? WHILE 1 /STRING REPEAT THEN
  DUP IF OVER C@ S" <>" ONE-OF? ELSE 0 THEN >R 2DROP R> IF 2DROP -1 EXIT THEN
  2DUP 0 ?DO DUP I + C@ [CHAR] | = IF DROP 2DROP UNLOOP -1 EXIT THEN LOOP DROP
  + 1- C@ [CHAR] & = ;
: PIECES-P ( closer --- )   \ a plain word: text, up to a blank, a ; or the closer - nothing quoted, no $ in it (899:
  \ a word's first character says what it is; texts and values are joined inside "...")
  GLOBW @ >R  0 GLOBW !  -1 BARE !  NDP @ SWAP T0
  BEGIN CUR OVER WORD-END? 0= WHILE
    CUR [CHAR] ` = IF S" `...` is sh's - $( ) captures a command's output" P-ERR THEN      \ (916)
    CUR [CHAR] $ = CUR [CHAR] ' = OR CUR [CHAR] " = OR IF
      CUR [CHAR] $ = IF S" a $ inside a plain word - a double-quoted text joins a value to text: $dir/file in quotes"
      ELSE S" a quote inside a plain word - a word is one thing; a double-quoted text joins texts" THEN P-ERR THEN
    GET DUP [CHAR] * = OVER [CHAR] ? = OR IF -1 GLOBW ! THEN T,   \ \ too (867): quotes are the one way to escape
  REPEAT DROP
  TXS @ TXP @ OVER - DUP 2 > IF + 2 - 2 S" ()" COMPARE 0= IF S" name() { } is sh's - var name {|params| ... } makes a function" P-ERR THEN ELSE 2DROP THEN   \ (916)
  TXP @ TXS @ - 2 > IF  TXS @ 2 S" <<" COMPARE 0= IF                                  \ (963)
    TXS @ 2 + C@ [CHAR] < = IF S" <<< is bash's - echo text | cmd, or << END and the lines" P-ERR THEN   \ (974)
    S" <<END and <<- are sh's - << END, blanks round it; an END indented takes that much off each line" P-ERR THEN THEN
  TXS @ TXP @ OVER - GLUED? IF S" an operator glued to a word - | > < & and 2> are words of their own, blanks round them" P-ERR THEN
  TXS @ TXP @ OVER - DUP 1 > IF  + 1- C@ [CHAR] \ =  CUR 10 = CUR 13 = OR AND
    IF S" a \ that continues the line is a word of its own - a blank before it" P-ERR THEN  ELSE 2DROP THEN   \ (906)
  T)
  DUP NDP @ = IF S" a word was expected" P-ERR THEN
  BARE @ IF DUP N+ NDP @ = IF DUP LITERAL? THEN THEN
  GLOBW @ IF 1 OVER 3 CELLS - CELL+ ! THEN  DROP  R> GLOBW ! ;
: TEXT-ALONE ( w --- p | 0 )   \ the word a text alone, its one piece
  N+ DUP @ N-TX = OVER N+ @ 0= AND 0= IF DROP 0 THEN ;
: MAP-KEY? ( w --- f )   \ a map's key: a text alone, ending in : after something - or a quoted word, its : read
  DUP @B IF DROP -1 EXIT THEN                       \ after it (975: a key with a blank had no way in a literal, though
  TEXT-ALONE DUP 0= IF EXIT THEN                    \ printed so, ["a b": 1] - it goes in so now, print-paste)
  DUP @B 1 > SWAP DUP @A SWAP @B + 1- C@ [CHAR] : = AND ;
: COLON? ( w --- f )   \ [:]'s word
  TEXT-ALONE DUP 0= IF EXIT THEN  DUP @B 1 = SWAP @A C@ [CHAR] : = AND ;
: MAP-ERR ( --- )   S" a map: key: value - each key k: or 'a b':" P-ERR ;
: KEY-CUT ( w --- )   DUP @B IF DROP EXIT THEN  -1 SWAP N+ 2 CELLS + +! ;   \ a plain key's text without its :
: NO-KEYS ( ls --- )   N+ BEGIN DUP @ WHILE DUP @B IF MAP-ERR THEN NSKIP REPEAT DROP ;   \ a list's: no "k": in it
VARIABLE QK#                                       \ the quoted keys read (975): a list's words looked at only if one was
: MAP? ( ls f --- )   \ the list read: [:] or [key: value ...] - a map, its keys without their :; f, a quoted key read in it
  >R  DUP N+ DUP @ 0= IF 2DROP R> DROP EXIT THEN
  DUP NSKIP @ 0= OVER COLON? AND IF DROP N-MP OVER ! N+ NDP ! N) R> DROP EXIT THEN
  DUP MAP-KEY? 0= IF DROP R> IF NO-KEYS ELSE DROP THEN EXIT THEN  R> DROP  N-MP ROT !
  BEGIN DUP @ WHILE  DUP MAP-KEY? 0= IF MAP-ERR THEN  DUP KEY-CUT  NSKIP
    DUP @ 0= IF MAP-ERR THEN  DUP @B IF MAP-ERR THEN  NSKIP  REPEAT DROP ;
: BS-WORD? ( w --- f )   DUP IF S" \" BARE= THEN ;     \ the word \ - the line goes on (906)
: BS-AT-END ( --- )   \ after a \ word only blanks or a comment before the line's end: the next line its command's too
  IN-POS @ BEGIN DUP IN-LEN @ < WHILE
    IN-TEXT @ OVER + C@ DUP BL = SWAP 9 = OR 0= IF
      IN-TEXT @ OVER + C@ DUP 10 = OVER 13 = OR SWAP [CHAR] # = OR IF DROP EXIT THEN
      DROP S" a \ word goes on to the next line - at a line's end; the text \ is '\'" P-ERR THEN
    1+ REPEAT
  DROP S" a \ at the end with no line after it" P-ERR ;
: LIST-P ( --- )   \ [ ... ]: a N-LS of its words - or a map
  QK# @ >R  NDP @  0 0 N-LS N,
  BEGIN -1 SKIP-WS CUR [CHAR] ] <> WHILE CUR 0= IF S" ] missing" P-ERR THEN
    NDP @ [CHAR] ] WORD-P  DUP BS-WORD? IF BS-AT-END NDP ! ELSE DROP THEN REPEAT   \ a \ at a line's end: as a command's (906)
  GET DROP N)  R> QK# @ <> MAP? ;
: BLOCK-P ( --- )   \ { |a b| ... }: a N-BK - its parameters' names as leaves, then its commands
  NDP @ 0 0 N-BK N,  0 SKIP-WS
  CUR [CHAR] | = IF GET DROP
    BEGIN 0 SKIP-WS CUR [CHAR] | <> WHILE
      CUR NAME0? 0= IF S" a block's parameters are names between | |" P-ERR THEN
      NAME-P N-TX N,  1 OVER CELL+ +!  REPEAT  GET DROP THEN
  DROP [CHAR] } DUP CMDS N) ;      \ } ends a word too, as ) and ] do (920): { echo $y} and }} had been refused
: WORD-ENDS ( closer --- )   \ after a word's form - ] } " ' a $name or $( ): its end, nothing glued (899)
  CUR SWAP WORD-END? 0= IF S" nothing right after a ] } quote or $value - a blank first; a double-quoted text joins texts" P-ERR THEN ;
VARIABLE CUR-CMD                                   \ the command being read, at this level (904)
: GOES-ON? ( w --- f )   DUP S" |" BARE= OVER S" &&" BARE= OR SWAP S" ||" BARE= OR ;
: ECHO-BLK ( closer --- closer )   \ a block, a word of echo's: bash's {a,b} - an error (976: it printed <block>)
  DUP [CHAR] ] = IF EXIT THEN  CUR-CMD @ ?DUP 0= IF EXIT THEN  N+ DUP NDP @ 3 CELLS - = IF DROP EXIT THEN
  DUP S" echo" BARE= 0= IF DROP EXIT THEN                       \ echo first, and no | && || & since: its own word
  BEGIN DUP NDP @ 3 CELLS - <> WHILE  DUP GOES-ON? OVER S" &" BARE= OR IF DROP EXIT THEN  NSKIP REPEAT DROP
  S" echo of a block - { } makes one: '{a,b}' is the text, quoted" P-ERR ;
: QKEY? ( closer wrd --- closer f )   \ a quoted word in [ ], a : glued and then its end: a map's key, marked (975)
  CUR [CHAR] : <> IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  OVER [CHAR] ] = IF  1 PK 2 PICK WORD-END? IF  GET DROP  1 SWAP 2 CELLS + !  1 QK# +!  -1 EXIT THEN THEN  DROP 0 ;
: WORD-P' ( closer --- )   \ one word: a N-WRD - what it is said by its first character (899)
  0 0 N-WRD N,
  CUR [CHAR] [ = IF GET DROP LIST-P IX? N) WORD-ENDS EXIT THEN
  CUR [CHAR] { = IF ECHO-BLK GET DROP BLOCK-P N) WORD-ENDS EXIT THEN
  CUR [CHAR] ( = 1 PK [CHAR] ( = AND IF S" arithmetic is $(( ))" P-ERR THEN     \ one way (867)
  CUR [CHAR] @ = IF GET DROP 0 0 N-SP N,
    CUR [CHAR] ( = IF GET DROP 0 0 N-CP N, [CHAR] ) DUP CMDS N) IX?
    ELSE CUR [CHAR] [ = IF GET DROP LIST-P IX?                        \ @[a b c]: a list written there, spread (918)
    ELSE CUR NAME0? 0= IF S" @ spreads a name, a [list] or a ( ) - not this" P-ERR THEN VAR-P THEN THEN  N) N) WORD-ENDS EXIT THEN
  CUR [CHAR] " = IF NDP @ 3 CELLS - >R GET DROP QUOTED-P R> QKEY? 0= IF IX? THEN N) WORD-ENDS EXIT THEN
  CUR [CHAR] ' = IF NDP @ 3 CELLS - >R GET DROP 0 0 N-QU N, SQUOTE-P N) R> QKEY? 0= IF IX? THEN N) WORD-ENDS EXIT THEN
  CUR [CHAR] $ = IF GET DROP DOLLAR-P IX? N) WORD-ENDS EXIT THEN
  PIECES-P N) ;
' WORD-P' IS WORD-P
: SET-FIRST? ( last --- f )   \ the command's first word set or append: its target next (append's too, 885)
  \ the first word is the node after the command's (950): after a \ at a line's end last is the command's node,
  \ and reading the kind three cells before it read before the nodes' block for a script's first command
  DUP 0= IF EXIT THEN  DUP CUR-CMD @ N+ = SWAP DUP S" set" BARE= OVER S" append" BARE= OR OVER S" read" BARE= OR SWAP S" del" BARE= OR AND ;
  \ append's and del's (976: gone) still, so their old words read as they were and the error can say where they went
: SET-TARGET-P ( closer --- )   \ set's target, after the command's first word set: read as after a $ (881)
  CUR NAME0? 0= IF WORD-P EXIT THEN  >R 0 0 N-WRD N, VAR-P N)
  CUR R> WORD-END? 0= IF S" a name, or name[key], to set" P-ERR THEN ;
\ ---- source file (890): read in place of its line, when the script is read - a top-level command
: SF-STACK ( --- addr )   SF-S @ ;
: SF-ROOM ( --- )   SF-N @ SF-CAP @ < IF EXIT THEN  SF-CAP @ 2* 8 MAX DUP SF-CAP !
  DUP 6 * CELLS SF-T @ SWAP RESIZE THROW SF-T !  5 * CELLS SF-S @ SWAP RESIZE THROW SF-S ! ;
VARIABLE SF-SP  VARIABLE SF-CUR                    \ how many below; the file being read
VARIABLE SF-SEEN  VARIABLE SF-MORE  VARIABLE TOP-CMD   \ sourced text so far, sized for; the top-level command
: LINES# ( c-addr u --- n )   1 ROT ROT  0 ?DO  DUP I + C@ 10 = IF SWAP 1+ SWAP THEN  LOOP DROP ;
: DIR$ ( c-addr u --- c-addr u' )   BEGIN DUP WHILE  2DUP + 1- C@ [CHAR] / = IF EXIT THEN  1- REPEAT ;
: SF-THERE? ( c-addr u --- f )   R/O OPEN-FILE IF DROP 0 ELSE CLOSE-FILE DROP -1 THEN ;
VARIABLE SFL-A  VARIABLE SFL-U
: SF-LIB ( c-addr u --- c-addr2 u2 | 0 0 )   \ a name with no /: in each directory of $RILL3_PATH, the first (924)
  S" RILL3_PATH" R-TEXT R-ENV  S" :" R-TEXT R-SPLIT                      ( c u dirs )
  DUP R-LEN 0 ?DO  DUP I R-AT R-ANY>TEXT R-T@ DUP IF
      S" /" CAT 4 PICK 4 PICK CAT  2DUP SF-THERE? IF SFL-U ! SFL-A ! DROP 2DROP SFL-A @ SFL-U @ UNLOOP EXIT THEN THEN  2DROP
  LOOP  DROP 2DROP 0 0 ;
: SF-PATH ( c-addr u --- c-addr2 u2 )   \ relative to the directory of the file sourcing it; a name with no
  OVER C@ [CHAR] / = IF EXIT THEN                                           \ / not there, $RILL3_PATH's (924)
  2DUP [CHAR] / SCAN NIP >R  2DUP SF-CUR @ SF$ DIR$ 2SWAP CAT                ( c u path pu )
  R> 0= IF 2DUP SF-THERE? 0= IF 2OVER SF-LIB DUP IF 2SWAP 2DROP 2SWAP 2DROP EXIT THEN 2DROP THEN THEN  2SWAP 2DROP ;
: SF-READ ( c-addr u --- addr len -1 | 0 )   \ a whole file, into the heap
  R/O OPEN-FILE IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN  >R
  R@ FILE-SIZE THROW DROP  DUP ALLOCATE THROW  DUP ROT R@ READ-FILE THROW  R> CLOSE-FILE DROP -1 ;
: HEAP$ ( c-addr u --- c-addr2 u )   DUP >R DUP ALLOCATE THROW DUP >R SWAP MOVE R> R> ;   \ a name kept past this compile
: SF-PUSH ( c-addr u --- )   \ the reader below kept; the file read from its start, its lines the next free
  SF-N @ SF-LINE0 @ ?DO  2DUP I SF$ COMPARE 0= IF 2DROP UNLOOP EXIT THEN  LOOP   \ sourced already: nothing more (924) -
                                                                         \ at the prompt, this line's: a later line reloads
  SF-ROOM
  2DUP SF-READ 0= IF S" source cannot open" 2SWAP ++ G-ERR THEN      ( name len text tlen )
  DUP SF-SEEN +!  SF-SEEN @ SF-MORE @ > IF  SF-SEEN @ SF-MORE !  DROP FREE DROP 2DROP -4106 THROW  THEN
  SF-SP @ 5 * CELLS SF-STACK +  IN-TEXT @ OVER !  IN-LEN @ OVER CELL+ !  IN-POS @ OVER 2 CELLS + !
    IN-LINE @ OVER 3 CELLS + !  SF-CUR @ SWAP 4 CELLS + !  1 SF-SP +!
  SF-N @ SF >R  SF-NEXT @ R@ !  2DUP LINES# DUP R@ CELL+ !  SF-NEXT +!  OVER R@ 4 CELLS + !  LN @ R@ 5 CELLS + !
  IN-LEN ! IN-TEXT !  HEAP$ R@ 3 CELLS + ! R@ 2 CELLS + !  0 IN-POS !  -1 HD-AT !  R> @ 1+ IN-LINE !  SF-N @ SF-CUR !  1 SF-N +! ;
: SF-POP ( --- )   -1 SF-SP +!  -1 HD-AT !  SF-SP @ 5 * CELLS SF-STACK +
  DUP @ IN-TEXT !  DUP CELL+ @ IN-LEN !  DUP 2 CELLS + @ IN-POS !  DUP 3 CELLS + @ IN-LINE !  4 CELLS + @ SF-CUR ! ;
: SOURCE-ERR ( --- )   S" source takes one file name" G-ERR ;
: TOP-END ( --- )   \ a top-level command just ended: source file read in its place, its nodes dropped
  TOP-CMD @ DUP N+ S" source" BARE= 0= IF DROP EXIT THEN
  DUP @A LN !  DUP N+ NSKIP  DUP @ 0= IF SOURCE-ERR THEN  DUP BARE? 0= IF SOURCE-ERR THEN
  DUP NSKIP @ IF SOURCE-ERR THEN  BARE$ SF-PATH  ROT NDP !  SF-PUSH ;
: LINE-REST ( i --- i' )   BEGIN DUP IN-LEN @ < WHILE IN-TEXT @ OVER + C@ 10 = IF EXIT THEN 1+ REPEAT ;
\ ---- here-documents (963): cmd << END - the lines after the line holding it, up to one that is END alone,
\ are cmd's stdin, $values in them as in "...", \$ and \\ the characters, " and @ as written; << 'END' or
\ << "END": all as written. END may be indented: that much is taken off each line. The body is read ahead
\ when the << is, its pieces the word's, as a "..."'s; the line's newline, when read, jumps past it (GET).
VARIABLE HD-D  VARIABLE HD-DU  VARIABLE HD-Q  VARIABLE HD-IND  VARIABLE HD-SP  VARIABLE HD-SL
: HD-BL? ( c --- f )   DUP BL = SWAP 9 = OR ;
: HD-DELIM ( closer --- closer )   \ the word after <<: END, 'END' or "END" - in HD-D, HD-DU, HD-Q
  >R  CUR [CHAR] ' = CUR [CHAR] " = OR DUP HD-Q !  IF
    GET HERE-IN  BEGIN CUR 2 PICK <> WHILE  CUR DUP 0= SWAP 10 = OR IF S" a here-document's quoted END is not closed" P-ERR THEN  GET DROP  REPEAT
    HERE-IN OVER -  GET DROP ROT DROP
  ELSE  HERE-IN  BEGIN CUR R@ WORD-END? 0= WHILE GET DROP REPEAT  HERE-IN OVER -  THEN
  DUP 0= IF S" << wants the word that ends the here-document" P-ERR THEN  HD-DU ! HD-D !  R> ;
: HD-SEEK ( start --- term | -1 )   \ from start: the line that is END alone, blanks round it - its start; its blanks
  BEGIN DUP IN-LEN @ < WHILE                                           \ before END in HD-IND
    DUP IN-TEXT @ + OVER LINE-REST 2 PICK -  0 >R
    BEGIN DUP IF OVER C@ HD-BL? ELSE 0 THEN WHILE 1 /STRING R> 1+ >R REPEAT
    BEGIN DUP IF 2DUP + 1- C@ DUP HD-BL? SWAP 13 = OR ELSE 0 THEN WHILE 1- REPEAT
    HD-D @ HD-DU @ COMPARE 0= IF R> HD-IND ! EXIT THEN  R> DROP
    LINE-REST 1+ REPEAT  DROP -1 ;
: BS-LINE? ( eol --- f )   \ the line ending at eol ends with a \ word: the line goes on (906)
  BEGIN DUP 0> IF DUP 1- IN-TEXT @ + C@ HD-BL? ELSE 0 THEN WHILE 1- REPEAT
  DUP 1 < IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN  DUP 1- IN-TEXT @ + C@ [CHAR] \ <> IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP 2 < IF DROP -1 EXIT THEN  2 - IN-TEXT @ + C@ DUP HD-BL? SWAP 10 = OR ;
: HD-EOL ( i --- eol )   \ i's line's end - after a \ at it, the next one's: the body comes after the command's lines
  BEGIN LINE-REST DUP IN-LEN @ < IF DUP BS-LINE? ELSE 0 THEN WHILE 1+ REPEAT ;
: HD-LS ( --- )   \ a body line's start: HD-IND blanks at most off it
  HD-IND @ 0 ?DO  CUR HD-BL? 0= IF LEAVE THEN  GET DROP  LOOP ;
: HD-BODY ( start term --- )   \ the body, start up to the END line at term: a N-QU's pieces - read as a "..." is,
  -1 IN-HD !  SWAP IN-POS !  0 0 N-QU N,  T0  HD-LS                \ but for " and the lines; as a '...' when END is quoted (969:
  BEGIN IN-POS @ OVER < WHILE                          \ it had followed sh's, \n two characters where "..." makes one)
    CUR 10 = IF GET T, HD-LS
    ELSE HD-Q @ IF GET T,
    ELSE CUR [CHAR] \ = IF QU-ESC
    ELSE CUR [CHAR] $ = IF QU-DOLLAR
    ELSE CUR QU-AT GET T, THEN THEN THEN THEN
  REPEAT DROP T) N)  0 IN-HD ! ;
: HEREDOC-P ( closer --- )   \ the word after <<: its body, read ahead - after this line, or the body before on it
  0 0 N-WRD N,  HD-DELIM  WORD-ENDS  IN-POS @ HD-SP !  IN-LINE @ HD-SL !
  IN-POS @ HD-EOL  DUP HD-AT @ = IF DROP HD-TO @ ELSE 1+ THEN                       ( start )
  DUP HD-SEEK  DUP 0< IF S" << " HD-D @ HD-DU @ CAT S" : no line after it that is " CAT HD-D @ HD-DU @ CAT
    S"  alone, the here-document's end" CAT P-ERR THEN                                ( start term )
  OVER HD-SP @ ?DO  IN-TEXT @ I + C@ 10 = IF 1 IN-LINE +! THEN  LOOP               \ its errors said at its lines
  DUP LINE-REST 1+ IN-LEN @ MIN >R  HD-BODY
  HD-SP @ HD-EOL HD-AT !  R> HD-TO !  HD-SP @ IN-POS !  HD-SL @ IN-LINE !  N) ;
: ELSE-WORD? ( i --- f )   \ else or elif at i, a word of its own
  IN-LEN @ OVER - 4 < IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  IN-TEXT @ OVER + 4 2DUP S" else" COMPARE 0= >R S" elif" COMPARE 0= R> OR 0= IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  4 + DUP IN-LEN @ < 0= IF DROP -1 EXIT THEN
  IN-TEXT @ + C@ DUP -1 BLANK? SWAP [CHAR] { = OR ;
: NEXT-ELSE? ( --- f )   \ past the newline at IN-POS - blanks, blank lines, comments - else or elif starts a line
  IN-POS @ DUP HD-AT @ = IF DROP HD-TO @ ELSE 1+ THEN  BEGIN DUP IN-LEN @ < WHILE   \ past the here-documents after it (963)
    IN-TEXT @ OVER + C@  -1 BLANK? IF 1+
    ELSE IN-TEXT @ OVER + C@ [CHAR] # = IF LINE-REST ELSE ELSE-WORD? EXIT THEN THEN
  REPEAT DROP 0 ;
: ELSE-ON? ( w --- f )   \ a newline that does not end the command: an if's, its last word a block, else or elif next
  DUP N+ @ N-BK = SWAP N+ NSKIP @ 0= AND 0= IF 0 EXIT THEN    \ (904: a newline ends a command - rule 1 - so
  CUR-CMD @ N+ S" if" BARE= 0= IF 0 EXIT THEN  NEXT-ELSE? ;   \ } then else on the next line had been two)
: HD-OP? ( last --- f )   DUP IF S" <<" BARE= THEN ;   \ the word before this one <<: this one its END (963)
VARIABLE GROUP-W   \ a block first in its part of a command: a group if the part ends with it (960) - sh's
\ { ...; }, made in place, return in it the function's as break and continue were the loop's: `cmd || { echo
\ no; return 1 }` had gone on. Marked as read, as a body is (MARK): a walk of every command's words in the scan
\ cost 1.5 % of a script's compiling - NSKIP goes through each word's nodes
: GROUP-END ( --- )   GROUP-W @ ?DUP IF N+ 1 SWAP 2 CELLS + !  0 GROUP-W ! THEN ;
: GROUP-NEXT ( last --- last )   \ before a word: the part ended - at the command's start, or && or || next - or not
  GROUP-W @ 0= IF EXIT THEN  DUP 0= IF GROUP-END EXIT THEN
  CUR [CHAR] & = 1 PK [CHAR] & = AND  CUR [CHAR] | = 1 PK [CHAR] | = AND OR IF GROUP-END ELSE 0 GROUP-W ! THEN ;
: GROUP? ( w last --- w )   \ after a word: a block with no parameters, at the command's start or after && or ||
  OVER N+ DUP @ N-BK = SWAP @A 0= AND 0= IF DROP EXIT THEN
  DUP IF  DUP CUR-CMD @ = IF DROP EXIT THEN   \ after a \ at a line's end: last is the command's node, not known
    DUP S" &&" BARE= SWAP S" ||" BARE= OR 0= IF EXIT THEN  ELSE DROP THEN  DUP GROUP-W ! ;
: CMDS' ( close closer --- )   \ commands up to close - 0, the text's end - each a N-CMD of its words; the
  CUR-CMD @ >R
  0 BEGIN  0 SKIP-WS CUR       \ third cell: 0, or the command's last word so far
    BEGIN  DUP 0= 4 PICK 0= AND  2 PICK SF-SP @ OR 0<> AND  WHILE    \ a top-level text's end: a sourced file's, back (890)
      DROP ?DUP IF N) TOP-END THEN  CUR 0= IF SF-SP @ IF SF-POP THEN THEN  0 0 SKIP-WS CUR  REPEAT
    DUP 0= IF DROP  2 PICK IF S" a closing bracket is missing" P-ERR THEN  IF N) THEN 2DROP GROUP-END R> CUR-CMD ! EXIT THEN
    DUP 4 PICK = IF DROP GET DROP  IF N) THEN 2DROP GROUP-END R> CUR-CMD ! EXIT THEN
    DUP 10 = 2 PICK BS-WORD? AND IF DROP GET DROP NDP ! CUR-CMD @      \ \ at the line's end: dropped, the line goes on
    ELSE DUP 10 = 2 PICK 0<> AND IF OVER GOES-ON? 2 PICK ELSE-ON? OR ELSE 0 THEN
    IF DROP GET DROP                                       \ after |, && or ||, or before else or elif: the line goes on
    ELSE DUP 10 = SWAP [CHAR] ; = OR IF GET DROP  IF N) OVER 0= IF TOP-END THEN THEN 0
    ELSE GROUP-NEXT  DUP 0= IF  2 PICK 0= IF NDP @ TOP-CMD ! THEN  NDP @ CUR-CMD !  IN-LINE @ 0 N-CMD N,  THEN
      DUP >R  DUP HD-OP? IF DROP 1 ELSE SET-FIRST? THEN >R  NDP @ OVER
      R> ?DUP IF 0> IF HEREDOC-P ELSE SET-TARGET-P THEN ELSE WORD-P THEN  R> GROUP?
      DUP BS-WORD? IF BS-AT-END THEN  THEN THEN THEN
  AGAIN ;
' CMDS' IS CMDS

\ ---- making Forth: the second pass, as cmc.py's Gen - frames, scopes and variables as records, cleared
: RC ( n --- addr )   CELLS RHP @ OVER + RHE @ > IF TOO-BIG THEN  RHP @ SWAP 2DUP ERASE RHP +! ;
: RH$ ( c-addr u --- c-addr2 u )   DUP 1 CELLS / 1+ RC  DUP >R SWAP DUP >R MOVE  R> R> SWAP ;   \ a name kept with the records (869)
VARIABLE FR  VARIABLE SC                           \ the frame and the scope being made
: NEW-FRAME ( kind --- f )   5 RC  TUCK !  1 OVER CELL+ ! ;   \ [kind: 0 main, 1 def, 2 block][slots][captures][them][room]
: CAP@ ( f i --- v )   CELLS SWAP 3 CELLS + @ + @ ;   \ a block's captures: an array grown as they come (891; 32 at most before)
: CAPS-GROW ( --- )   FR @ 4 CELLS + @ 2* 8 MAX  DUP RC  FR @ 3 CELLS + @ OVER FR @ 2 CELLS + @ CELLS MOVE
  FR @ 3 CELLS + !  FR @ 4 CELLS + ! ;
: F-SLOT ( f --- n )   CELL+ DUP @  1 ROT +! ;
: SCOPE( ( --- )   2 RC  SC @ OVER !  SC ! ;      \ [parent][variables]
: )SCOPE ( --- )   SC @ @ SC ! ;
: VAR+ ( c-addr u slot boxed --- v )   \ [next][name][length][frame][slot][boxed][hoisted][function], in this scope
  \ and frame - hoisted (929): -1 known from the script's start, its var not yet met, 1 met; function: a block written to it
  2SWAP RH$ 2SWAP  8 RC >R  R@ 5 CELLS + !  R@ 4 CELLS + !  R@ 2 CELLS + !  R@ CELL+ !  FR @ R@ 3 CELLS + !
  SC @ CELL+ DUP @ R@ !  R@ SWAP !  R> ;
: DECLARE ( c-addr u boxed --- v )   FR @ F-SLOT SWAP VAR+ ;
: V-SLOT ( v --- n )   4 CELLS + @ ;
: VAR-IN ( c-addr u list --- v | 0 )   \ the variable of that name in one scope's list
  BEGIN ?DUP WHILE  >R 2DUP R@ CELL+ @ R@ 2 CELLS + @ COMPARE 0= IF 2DROP R> EXIT THEN  R> @ REPEAT 2DROP 0 ;
: FIND-VAR ( c-addr u --- v | 0 )   \ in this scope or any around it
  SC @ BEGIN ?DUP WHILE  >R 2DUP R@ CELL+ @ VAR-IN ?DUP IF NIP NIP R> DROP EXIT THEN  R> @ REPEAT 2DROP 0 ;
: CAP-INDEX ( v --- i )   \ v's place in this block's captures - added if new
  FR @ @ 2 <> IF  S" $" S| ROT DUP CELL+ @ SWAP 2 CELLS + @ CAT
    S" : a def sees only its parameters and its own variables (v0)" CAT G-ERR THEN
  FR @ 2 CELLS + @ 0 ?DO  FR @ I CAP@ OVER = IF DROP I UNLOOP EXIT THEN  LOOP
  FR @ 2 CELLS + @ FR @ 4 CELLS + @ = IF CAPS-GROW THEN
  FR @ 2 CELLS + @ TUCK CELLS FR @ 3 CELLS + @ + !  1 FR @ 2 CELLS + +! ;
VARIABLE SESSION   VARIABLE MAIN-FR   VARIABLE MAIN-SC   \ the prompt's session (869)
: MAIN-V? ( v --- f )   \ the script's variable, seen from a def (884) - or a top-level one, from anywhere (929)
  DUP 3 CELLS + @ MAIN-FR @ =  SWAP 6 CELLS + @  FR @ @ 1 = OR  AND ;
: REF ( v --- c-addr u )   \ v's cell - its value, unboxed: in this frame's slots, the main frame's, or this block's captures
  DUP 3 CELLS + @ FR @ = IF V-SLOT T# T" LS@" ++ EXIT THEN
  DUP MAIN-V? IF V-SLOT T# T" MLS@" ++ EXIT THEN  CAP-INDEX T# T" E@" ++ ;
: READ$ ( c-addr u --- c-addr2 u2 )   \ $name
  2DUP FIND-VAR ?DUP IF NIP NIP DUP REF ROT 5 CELLS + @ IF T" UPV@" ++ THEN EXIT THEN
  2DUP S" status" COMPARE 0= IF 2DROP T" STATUS @ D-NUM" EXIT THEN
  2DUP S" env" COMPARE 0= IF 2DROP T" ENV-BOX" EXIT THEN          \ $env[NAME] (870)
  2DUP S" args" COMPARE 0= IF 2DROP T" SCRIPT-ARGS" EXIT THEN     \ the script's arguments, a list (870)
  2DUP S" job" COMPARE 0= IF 2DROP T" JOB @ D-NUM" EXIT THEN       \ the last job & started, for wait $job (905)
  S" no variable $" S| 2SWAP CAT S" - var makes one" ++ G-ERR ;
: OUT+ ( c-addr u --- )   \ to the output, a blank after it
  DUP OUP @ + 1+ OUE @ > IF TOO-BIG THEN  OUP @ SWAP DUP >R MOVE  R> OUP +!  BL OUP @ C!  1 OUP +! ;
: TK-IDX ( c-addr u --- i )   DROP 1+ DUP C@ 16 LSHIFT OVER 1+ C@ 8 LSHIFT OR SWAP 2 + C@ OR ;   \ a made word's number, from its call
: T-TICK$ ( c-addr u --- c-addr2 u2 )   TK-IDX T-TICK ;   \ its xt, from its call
: T-DEF ( name u body u --- c-addr u )   2SWAP TK-IDX T-BEGIN 2SWAP ++ T-END ++ ;   \ D i body F
: DEF-WORD ( c-addr u c-addr2 u2 --- )   T-DEF OUT+ ;   \ a made word: its tokens, to the output (926: had been : name body ;)
\ The words made - a loop's body, a block, a capture, a def's body, the script's main - were Forth words with
\ names (B1.1, D2.2 ..., in a word list of 256 threads, 909); now they are numbered per compile, no name.
: FRESH ( c-addr u --- c-addr2 u2 )   2DROP GEN-NEW T-CALL ;   \ a made word: its call (926) - the letter not used
: PLAIN-C? ( c --- f )   DUP 32 127 WITHIN SWAP [CHAR] " <> AND ;   \ no " and nothing past printable ASCII: S" holds it
: PLAIN? ( c-addr u --- f )   -1 ROT ROT 0 ?DO  DUP I + C@ PLAIN-C?  ROT AND SWAP  LOOP DROP ;
: PLAIN# ( c-addr u --- n )   200 MIN DUP 0 ?DO  OVER I + C@ PLAIN-C? 0= IF DROP I LEAVE THEN  LOOP NIP ;   \ S" can hold so many
: SQ$ ( c-addr u --- c-addr2 u2 )   T-STR ;   \ a text's token (926: had been S" text")
: TEXT-CODE ( c-addr u --- c-addr2 u2 )   \ S" text" TXT - or, past 200 characters or with a " or a control
  \ character, in pieces: TXT( runs - TXT+ - and characters - TXT-C - )TXT. S" holds 255 at most: a longer
  \ text had been cm: error -256, or at the prompt a wrong text; and every character of one with a " in it
  \ had gone on the data stack (891)
  2DUP PLAIN? OVER 201 < AND IF  SQ$ T" TXT" ++ EXIT THEN
  T" TXT(" TOP$ 2SWAP
  BEGIN DUP WHILE
    2DUP PLAIN# ?DUP IF  >R OVER R@ SQ$ T" TXT+" ++  ELSE  OVER C@ T# T" TXT-C" ++  1 >R  THEN   ( acc u t tu p pu )
    2SWAP R> /STRING SWAP >R >R  SEQ+  R> R> SWAP
  REPEAT 2DROP  T" )TXT" SEQ+ ;
: UPPER ( c-addr u --- c-addr2 u )   S| 2DUP OVER + SWAP ?DO I C@ [CHAR] a [CHAR] z 1+ WITHIN IF I C@ 32 - I C! THEN LOOP ;

\ ---- words and their kinds
: WORDS-END ( w --- end )   BEGIN DUP @ WHILE NSKIP REPEAT ;
: CHAR-AT ( c-addr u c --- k )   \ where c first is, or u
  >R 0 BEGIN 2DUP > WHILE 2 PICK OVER + C@ R@ = IF NIP NIP R> DROP EXIT THEN 1+ REPEAT NIP NIP R> DROP ;
: IN-LIST? ( c-addr u list u2 --- f )   \ the text one of the list's words
  BEGIN DUP 0> WHILE
    2DUP BL CHAR-AT >R  2OVER 3 PICK R@ COMPARE 0= IF R> DROP 2DROP 2DROP -1 EXIT THEN  R> 1+ /STRING
  REPEAT 2DROP 2DROP 0 ;
: HABIT-NAME? ( c-addr u --- f )   DUP 0= IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN  OVER C@ NAME0? ROT ROT 0 ?DO DUP I + C@ NAMEC? ROT AND SWAP LOOP DROP ;
: SH-SAYS ( c-addr u advice-a advice-u --- )   2SWAP S| S"  is sh's - " CAT 2SWAP CAT G-ERR ;
: SH-HABIT ( c-addr u --- )   \ a first word that is sh's and no program here: an error that says this language's way (916)
  2DUP S" export" COMPARE 0= IF S" $env set NAME value" SH-SAYS THEN
  2DUP S" local declare typeset" IN-LIST? IF S" var name value - a function's variables are its own" SH-SAYS THEN
  2DUP S" unset" COMPARE 0= IF S" $m del key, $env del NAME" SH-SAYS THEN
  2DUP S" function alias" IN-LIST? IF S" var name {|params| ... }" SH-SAYS THEN
  2DUP S" then fi do done esac" IN-LIST? IF S" blocks: if cond { }, while cond { }, for x values { }, case v { }" SH-SAYS THEN
  2DUP [CHAR] = SCAN NIP IF  2DUP 2DUP [CHAR] = SCAN NIP - HABIT-NAME? IF S" var x 5 makes a variable, set x 5 changes one, $env set X 5 the environment" SH-SAYS THEN THEN
  2DROP ;
: FIND-FN ( c-addr u --- f )   FIND-VAR DUP IF 7 CELLS + @ 0<> THEN ;   \ a variable a block was written to: a function (929)
: BUILTIN? ( c-addr u --- f )   \ a builtin's name: a first word so is that builtin, before any function's
  S" var set put echo append if for while break continue return range true false each cd exit wait read kind source glob del case trap forth run" IN-LIST? ;
  \ append and del are gone (976) but kept here, so the first word says where they went
: PROGRAM? ( w --- f )   \ a first word that names no builtin and no def: a program - unless it is sh's (916)
  DUP BARE? 0= IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN  BARE$
  2DUP S" run" COMPARE 0= IF 2DROP -1 EXIT THEN       \ run prog words: a program's stage, the program a value (967)
  2DUP BUILTIN? IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN  2DUP FIND-FN IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN  SH-HABIT -1 ;
: ANDOR? ( w --- w f )   DUP S" &&" BARE= OVER S" ||" BARE= OR ;   \ && or || between commands
: CHAIN-ANDOR ( from to --- w )   \ in if's or while's command: && and || in a condition are the condition's (914)
  SWAP -1 >R
  BEGIN 2DUP <> WHILE
    DUP N+ @ N-BK = IF R> DROP 0 >R ELSE
    DUP S" elif" BARE= IF R> DROP -1 >R ELSE
    R@ 0= IF ANDOR? IF NIP R> DROP EXIT THEN THEN THEN THEN
    NSKIP REPEAT DROP R> DROP ;
: TO-ANDOR ( from to --- w )   \ the first && or || between commands - if a && b { } had been if a, then b { } (914)
  OVER S" if" BARE= 2 PICK S" while" BARE= OR IF CHAIN-ANDOR EXIT THEN
  SWAP BEGIN 2DUP <> WHILE ANDOR? IF NIP EXIT THEN NSKIP REPEAT DROP ;
: TO-PIPE ( from to --- w )   SWAP BEGIN 2DUP <> WHILE DUP S" |" BARE= IF NIP EXIT THEN NSKIP REPEAT DROP ;
: TO-BLOCK ( from to --- w )   SWAP BEGIN 2DUP <> WHILE DUP N+ @ N-BK = IF NIP EXIT THEN NSKIP REPEAT DROP ;
: LAST-W ( from to --- w )   >R BEGIN DUP NSKIP R@ <> WHILE NSKIP REPEAT R> DROP ;
: LAST-STAGE ( from to --- w )   SWAP BEGIN 2DUP SWAP TO-PIPE DUP 3 PICK = IF DROP NIP EXIT THEN NIP NSKIP AGAIN ;
: TWO? ( from to --- f )   2DUP = IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN  SWAP NSKIP 2DUP = IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN  NSKIP = ;
: NAMED? ( c-addr u c-addr2 u2 --- c-addr u f )   2OVER COMPARE 0= ;

\ ---- values
DEFER PIECE ( p --- c-addr u )   DEFER BODY-CODE ( cmd --- c-addr u )   DEFER CMD-RANGE ( from to --- c-addr u )
DEFER PIPELINE ( from to c-addr u --- c-addr2 u2 )
DEFER IX-CODE ( c-addr u ix --- c-addr2 u2 )   \ a value's keys, each CM-AT (913): below, once WORD-CODE is
: PIECE-IX ( p --- c-addr u p' )   \ a piece's code - indexed, when keys follow it (914: in "...", $(cmd)[k] too)
  DUP >R PIECE R> NSKIP  DUP @ N-IX = IF DUP >R IX-CODE R> NSKIP THEN ;
: PIECES ( p --- c-addr u )   \ pieces to their END: the first's value and D-STR, each next's and JOIN
  PIECE-IX >R T" D-STR" ++ TOP$ R>  BEGIN DUP @ WHILE  PIECE-IX >R T" JOIN" ++ SEQ+ R>  REPEAT DROP ;
: WORD-CODE ( w --- c-addr u )   \ its value - indexed, when keys follow it (913)
  N+ DUP NSKIP DUP @ N-IX = IF >R PIECE R> IX-CODE EXIT THEN DROP  DUP NSKIP @ IF PIECES ELSE PIECE THEN ;
: IX-CODE' ( c-addr u ix --- c-addr2 u2 )   N+ BEGIN DUP @ WHILE DUP >R WORD-CODE ++ T" CM-AT" ++ R> NSKIP REPEAT DROP ;
' IX-CODE' IS IX-CODE
: GPIECE ( p --- c-addr u )   DUP @ N-TX = IF PIECE ELSE PIECE T" GLOB-ESC" ++ THEN ;   \ a $'s, a quote's: no wildcards
: GLOB-CODE ( w --- c-addr u )   \ a glob's pattern: its unquoted texts as they are, the rest escaped (881)
  N+ DUP GPIECE T" D-STR" ++ TOP$ ROT NSKIP BEGIN DUP @ WHILE DUP >R GPIECE T" JOIN" ++ SEQ+ R> NSKIP REPEAT DROP ;
: CAP-CMD ( cp --- from to -1 | 0 )   \ a capture of one command: its words
  N+ DUP @ N-CMD <> IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN  DUP NSKIP @ IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN  N+ DUP WORDS-END -1 ;
: PROGRAM-LAST? ( from to --- f )   2DUP LAST-STAGE TUCK = IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN  NIP PROGRAM? ;   \ its last stage a program
: PROG-CAP? ( cp --- f )   \ $( ) of one command, a pipeline ending in a program
  CAP-CMD 0= IF 0 EXIT THEN  2DUP TO-ANDOR OVER <> IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN  PROGRAM-LAST? ;
: PROG-LIST? ( cp --- f )   \ one command, && or || in it, its last pipeline ending in a program (960)
  CAP-CMD 0= IF 0 EXIT THEN  2DUP TO-ANDOR OVER = IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  BEGIN 2DUP TO-ANDOR 2DUP <> WHILE ROT DROP NSKIP SWAP REPEAT DROP  PROGRAM-LAST? ;
: PIPE-CAP ( cp c-addr u --- c-addr2 u2 )   \ that pipeline, ended so (859, 862)
  LN @ >R  ROT N+ DUP @A LN !  N+ DUP WORDS-END 2SWAP PIPELINE  R> LN ! ;
: CAPTURE-WORD ( cp --- c-addr u )   \ a word of its own for the capture's commands: its name
  S" C" FRESH ROT SCOPE( N+ BODY-CODE )SCOPE 2OVER 2SWAP DEF-WORD ;
: NO-TRANSFER? ( node --- f )   \ no break, continue or return in it: a capture of it needs no CATCH (878)
  DUP S" break" BARE-IN? OVER S" continue" BARE-IN? OR SWAP S" return" BARE-IN? OR 0= ;
: TEXT-CAP ( cp --- c-addr u )   \ what the commands print, one text
  DUP NO-TRANSFER? >R CAPTURE-WORD T-TICK$  R> IF T" CAPTURE-TEXT-P" ELSE T" CAPTURE-TEXT" THEN ++ ;
: SPREAD-CODE ( p --- c-addr u )   \ what @ spreads: a list
  DUP @ N-CP = IF DUP PROG-CAP? IF T" PIPE-LINES" PIPE-CAP EXIT THEN
    DUP PROG-LIST? IF TEXT-CAP T" TEXT-LINES" ++ EXIT THEN   \ @(cd d && find .): the lines too, not to the terminal
    CAPTURE-WORD T-TICK$ T" CAPTURE" ++ EXIT THEN  PIECE ;
: ARG-CODE ( w --- c-addr u )   DUP N+ @ N-SP = IF N+ N+ DUP NSKIP DUP @ N-IX = IF   \ @(cmd)[k]: its values' k-th,
    >R SPREAD-CODE R> IX-CODE T" ARG@1" ++ EXIT THEN  DROP SPREAD-CODE T" ARG@" ++ EXIT THEN   \ spread if a list (913)
  DUP @A IF GLOB-CODE T" GLOB ARG@" ++ EXIT THEN  WORD-CODE T" ARG" ++ ;   \ a word with * or ?: its paths (872)
: ARGS-CODE ( from to --- c-addr u )   \ ARGL, then each word's value ARG - a spread's list ARG@
  >R >R T" ARGL" TOP$  BEGIN R> R> 2DUP >R >R <> WHILE  R> DUP NSKIP >R ARG-CODE SEQ+ REPEAT  R> R> 2DROP ;
VARIABLE AP                                        \ the next of (( ))'s nodes
: AOP? ( c-addr u --- f )   AP @ @ N-OP = IF AP @ @A AP @ @B COMPARE 0= ELSE 2DROP 0 THEN ;
: A-TAKE ( --- c-addr u )   S" D" S| AP @ @A AP @ @B CAT T-NAMED  AP @ N+ AP ! ;   \ the operator taken: D and it
DEFER A-OR ( --- c-addr u )
: NUM-CODE ( p --- c-addr u )   \ a number: a cell, or boxed from 2^61 up (923)
  @A DUP T# ROT  1 61 LSHIFT DUP NEGATE 1+ SWAP WITHIN IF T" D-NUM" ELSE T" N>ITEM-D" THEN ++ ;
: A-PRIM ( --- c-addr u )
  AP @ DUP @ 0= IF S" (( )) ends too soon" G-ERR THEN  DUP NSKIP AP !
  DUP @ N-NM = IF NUM-CODE EXIT THEN
  DUP @ N-CP = IF  DUP PROG-CAP? 0= OVER NO-TRANSFER? AND IF                    \ an operand's $( ): its number,
    CAPTURE-WORD T-TICK$ T" CAPTURE-NUM" ++ EXIT THEN THEN                   \ if all it made, held (964)
  DUP @ N-OP <> IF PIECE EXIT THEN
  DUP @A OVER @B S" (" COMPARE 0= IF DROP A-OR S" )" AOP? 0= IF S" ) missing in (( ))" G-ERR THEN  AP @ N+ AP ! EXIT THEN
  DUP @A OVER @B S" -" COMPARE 0= IF DROP RECURSE T" D-NEG" ++ EXIT THEN
  DUP @A OVER @B S" !" COMPARE 0= IF DROP RECURSE T" D-LOGIC? 0= D-BOOL" ++ EXIT THEN
  S" in (( )):" S| ROT DUP @A SWAP @B ++ S" where a value goes" ++ G-ERR ;
: A-MUL ( --- c-addr u )   A-PRIM  BEGIN S" *" AOP? S" /" AOP? OR S" %" AOP? OR WHILE A-TAKE A-PRIM 2SWAP ++ ++ REPEAT ;
: A-ADD ( --- c-addr u )   A-MUL  BEGIN S" +" AOP? S" -" AOP? OR WHILE A-TAKE A-MUL 2SWAP ++ ++ REPEAT ;
: A-CMP ( --- c-addr u )   A-ADD
  S" ==" AOP? S" !=" AOP? OR S" <" AOP? OR S" <=" AOP? OR S" >" AOP? OR S" >=" AOP? OR IF A-TAKE A-ADD 2SWAP ++ ++ THEN ;
: A-AND ( --- c-addr u )   A-CMP
  BEGIN S" &&" AOP? WHILE AP @ N+ AP !  T" D-LOGIC? IF" ++ A-CMP ++ T" D-LOGIC? D-BOOL ELSE FALSE-BOX THEN" ++ REPEAT ;
: A-OR' ( --- c-addr u )   A-AND
  BEGIN S" ||" AOP? WHILE AP @ N+ AP !  T" D-LOGIC? IF TRUE-BOX ELSE" ++ A-AND ++ T" D-LOGIC? D-BOOL THEN" ++ REPEAT ;
' A-OR' IS A-OR
: A-PAREN? ( p --- f )   DUP @ N-OP = IF DUP @A SWAP @B 1 = SWAP C@ DUP [CHAR] ( = SWAP [CHAR] ) = OR AND ELSE DROP 0 THEN ;
: A-ONE ( ar --- p | 0 )   \ (( )) of one value, in parentheses or not: its node
  0 SWAP N+ BEGIN DUP @ WHILE  DUP A-PAREN? 0= IF  DUP @ N-OP = 2 PICK OR IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN  NIP DUP  THEN  NSKIP REPEAT DROP ;
: ARITH ( ar --- c-addr u )   AP @ >R  DUP A-ONE >R  N+ AP !  A-OR  AP @ @ IF S" in (( )): more than one expression" G-ERR THEN
  R> ?DUP IF @ N-NM <> IF T" D-ONE" ++ THEN THEN  R> AP ! ;   \ one value: a number, or a boolean (965, D-ONE)
: KEY-CODE ( w --- c-addr u )   DUP @B IF WORD-CODE ELSE BARE$ TEXT-CODE THEN ;   \ "a b": a quoted word's (975)
: MAP-CODE ( mp --- c-addr u )
  T" R-NEW-RECORD K-REC R-BOX" TOP$ ROT N+
  BEGIN DUP @ WHILE  >R T" DUP" R@ KEY-CODE ++  R> NSKIP DUP >R WORD-CODE ++ T" D-SET" ++ SEQ+  R> NSKIP REPEAT DROP ;
VARIABLE CAPS  VARIABLE CAPS#  VARIABLE CAPS-CAP   \ the names some block refers to: those variables boxed (866) -
: CAPS+ ( c-addr u --- )   \ grown as they come (891; 512 at most before)
  CAPS# @ CAPS-CAP @ = IF  CAPS-CAP @ 2* 16 MAX DUP CAPS-CAP !  2* RC  CAPS @ OVER CAPS# @ 2* CELLS MOVE  CAPS !  THEN
  CAPS @ CAPS# @ 2* CELLS + TUCK CELL+ ! !  1 CAPS# +! ;
: CAPTURED? ( c-addr u --- f )   \ at the prompt every variable of the session's own is boxed: a later line may capture it
  SESSION @ FR @ MAIN-FR @ = AND IF 2DROP -1 EXIT THEN
  CAPS# @ 0 ?DO  2DUP CAPS @ I 2* CELLS + DUP @ SWAP CELL+ @ COMPARE 0= IF 2DROP -1 UNLOOP EXIT THEN  LOOP 2DROP 0 ;
: NAME-LEN ( c-addr u --- k )   0 BEGIN 2DUP > IF 2 PICK OVER + C@ NAMEC? ELSE 0 THEN WHILE 1+ REPEAT NIP NIP ;
: OWN-PARAM? ( c-addr u bk --- f )   \ one of the block's own parameters (929)
  N+ BEGIN DUP @ N-TX = WHILE  >R 2DUP R@ @A R@ @B COMPARE 0= IF 2DROP R> DROP -1 EXIT THEN  R> N+ REPEAT DROP 2DROP 0 ;
VARIABLE SCAN-BK
: SCAN-BLOCK ( bk --- )   \ $names in a block's code - set's and append's targets are N-VRs (881, 885) - but its own
  DUP SCAN-BK !  DUP NSKIP SWAP N+                 \ parameters (929): a nested block's use of one is scanned there
  BEGIN 2DUP <> WHILE
    DUP @ N-VR = IF DUP @A OVER @B 2DUP SCAN-BK @ OWN-PARAM? IF 2DROP ELSE CAPS+ THEN THEN
    DUP @ N-CMD = IF DUP N+ DUP BARE? IF BARE$ 2DUP HABIT-NAME? IF CAPS+ ELSE 2DROP THEN ELSE DROP THEN THEN   \ a function called by
  N+ REPEAT 2DROP ;                               \ its name is a use of its variable too (930): a local one calling itself
: MARK ( w --- )   N+ DUP @ N-BK = IF 1 SWAP 2 CELLS + ! ELSE DROP THEN ;   \ a body made in place, or in its own frame
: MARK-CMD ( cmd --- )   \ if's, elif's and else's bodies, a loop's, a def's: no value, nothing captured
  N+ DUP S" if" BARE= IF  BEGIN DUP @ WHILE DUP MARK NSKIP REPEAT DROP EXIT THEN
  DUP S" while" BARE= OVER S" for" BARE= OR IF  DUP WORDS-END LAST-W MARK EXIT THEN  DROP ;
: SCAN-CAPS ( --- )   0 CAPS# !
  ND0 @ BEGIN DUP NDP @ U< WHILE DUP @ N-CMD = IF DUP MARK-CMD THEN N+ REPEAT DROP
  ND0 @ BEGIN DUP NDP @ U< WHILE DUP @ N-BK = OVER @B 0= AND IF DUP SCAN-BLOCK THEN N+ REPEAT DROP ;
: PARAMS ( node --- node' mask )   \ a block's or def's parameters declared, the bits of those a block captures
  0 0 ROT BEGIN DUP @ N-TX = WHILE
    DUP @A OVER @B 2DUP CAPTURED? DUP >R DECLARE DROP
    R> IF ROT 1 3 PICK LSHIFT OR ROT ROT THEN  SWAP 1+ SWAP  N+ REPEAT  NIP SWAP ;
: BLOCK-CODE ( bk --- c-addr u )   \ a block: a word with a frame of its own - made, with its captures
  DUP S" break" BARE-IN? OVER S" continue" BARE-IN? OR >R        \ a break or continue may leave it: a guard (931)
  FR @ >R  2 NEW-FRAME FR !  SCOPE(
  DUP S" return" BARE-IN? IF S" %def" 0 0 VAR+ DROP THEN      \ return ends the block, a function (929)
  DUP N+ PARAMS >R
  S" B" FRESH 2SWAP BODY-CODE
  2 PICK S" return" BARE-IN? IF  S" B" FRESH 2SWAP 2OVER 2SWAP T-DEF OUT+
    T-TICK$ T" BLK-TAIL" ++  T" ACT-PUSH D-NUM 0 LS!" 2SWAP ++  THEN
  ROT @A >R  2OVER TK-IDX T-BEGIN  T" [ 0 R-MARK ]" ++  FR @ CELL+ @ T#++ T" FRAME" ++   \ its binding no line: the call's said
  R> T# R> T#++ T" BIND-K" ++ ++  2SWAP ++ T" UNFRAME" ++ T-END ++ OUT+   \ its arguments on the stack (930)
  FR @ )SCOPE R> FR !
  R> IF  >R  S" B" FRESH 2SWAP T-TICK$ T" BLK-GUARD" ++  2OVER 2SWAP T-DEF OUT+  R>  THEN   \ guarded: its word inside (931)
  0 0 TOP$ 2 PICK 2 CELLS + @ 0 ?DO  2 PICK I CAP@ REF SEQ+  LOOP
  ROT 2 CELLS + @ T#++ 2SWAP T-TICK$ ++ T" BLK-NEW" ++ ;
: PIECE' ( p --- c-addr u )
  DUP @ CASE
    N-TX OF DUP @A SWAP @B TEXT-CODE ENDOF
    N-NM OF NUM-CODE ENDOF
    N-BO OF @A IF T" TRUE-BOX" ELSE T" FALSE-BOX" THEN ENDOF
    N-VR OF DUP @A OVER @B READ$ ROT IX-CODE' ENDOF
    N-QU OF N+ DUP @ IF PIECES ELSE DROP 0 0 TEXT-CODE THEN ENDOF
    N-CP OF DUP PROG-CAP? IF T" PIPE-TEXT" PIPE-CAP ELSE TEXT-CAP THEN ENDOF
    N-AR OF ARITH ENDOF
    N-LS OF N+ DUP WORDS-END ARGS-CODE ENDOF
    N-MP OF MAP-CODE ENDOF
    N-BK OF BLOCK-CODE ENDOF
    S" @ spreads into a command's words or a list - not here" G-ERR
  ENDCASE ;
' PIECE' IS PIECE
VARIABLE CHK   \ compiling a statement's commands, not a condition's: ?FAIL after them (927)
: CMD-CODE ( cmd --- c-addr u )   \ its code after [ line R-MARK ]: an error in it says its line (887)
  CHK @ >R -1 CHK !  DUP @A LN !  T" [" LN @ T#++ T" R-MARK ]" ++  ROT N+ DUP WORDS-END CMD-RANGE ++  R> CHK ! ;
: BODY-CODE' ( cmd --- c-addr u )   \ each command's Forth, to the END
  LN @ >R  0 0 TOP$ ROT BEGIN DUP @ WHILE DUP >R CMD-CODE SEQ+ R> NSKIP REPEAT DROP  R> LN ! ;
' BODY-CODE' IS BODY-CODE

\ ---- commands
: OK$ ( c-addr u --- c-addr2 u2 )   T" 0 STATUS !" ++ ;   \ a builtin done: status 0, as every command sets one (869)
: FLAG0 ( from to --- c-addr u )   \ a condition: ! ..., a value alone, or a command's status (859)
  2DUP = IF S" a condition was expected" G-ERR THEN
  2DUP TO-ANDOR OVER <> IF CMD-RANGE T" STATUS @ 0=" ++ EXIT THEN     \ a && b, ! a || b: the chain's status (914)
  OVER S" !" BARE= IF SWAP NSKIP SWAP RECURSE T" 0=" ++ EXIT THEN
  OVER NSKIP OVER = 2 PICK N+ @ N-TX <> AND IF DROP WORD-CODE T" D-COND" ++ EXIT THEN     \ true or false only (876)
  CMD-RANGE T" STATUS @ 0=" ++ ;
\ A command that fails ends a script (927, the owner's): after a statement's command - the last of a chain
\ of && and ||, if it ran - ?FAIL. Not when its status is tested: a condition of if, elif or while, a
\ chain's commands but its last, a ! command - and what they call, as long as they run (TESTING, counted at
\ run time). CHK: compiling a statement's commands, not a condition's. At the prompt nothing ends.
\ (CHK: above CMD-CODE)
: FLAG ( from to --- c-addr u )   CHK @ >R 0 CHK !  FLAG0  R> CHK !  T" TESTING+" 2SWAP ++ T" TESTING-" ++ ;
: INLINE ( w --- c-addr u )   \ a block with no parameters, its commands made in place
  N+ DUP @ N-BK <> OVER @A OR IF S" a block with no parameters was expected" G-ERR THEN  SCOPE( N+ BODY-CODE )SCOPE ;
: ELSE-ERR ( --- )   S" else { ... }" G-ERR ;
\ case value { patterns... { ... } ... } (910): each line of its block an arm - patterns, then a block; the first
\ arm one of whose patterns matches the value's text runs, as sh's case; none, status 0. A plain word is the
\ pattern as written - its * and ? a pattern's, not globbed - else its value's text, matched as match does
: CASE-ERR ( --- )   S" case value { patterns... { ... } } - an arm a line: patterns, then a block" G-ERR ;
: PAT-CODE ( w --- c-addr u )   DUP BARE? IF BARE$ TEXT-CODE ELSE WORD-CODE THEN  T" D-TEXT" ++ ;
VARIABLE ARM-1ST
: ARM-WORD ( acc u w --- acc u w' )   \ from w, one arm - patterns, then a block - its code added; arms a line
  -1 ARM-1ST !                        \ each, or several on one: 2 { a } * { b }
  BEGIN  DUP @ 0= IF CASE-ERR THEN  DUP N+ @ N-BK <> WHILE
    >R  ARM-1ST @ IF T" DUP" ELSE T" OVER" THEN  R@ PAT-CODE ++  ARM-1ST @ IF T" R-GLOB?" ELSE T" R-GLOB? OR" THEN ++
    0 ARM-1ST !  SEQ+  R> NSKIP  REPEAT
  ARM-1ST @ IF CASE-ERR THEN  DUP N+ NSKIP @ IF CASE-ERR THEN
  DUP >R INLINE  T" IF DROP" 2SWAP ++ T" ELSE" ++ SEQ+  R> NSKIP ;
: CASE-CMD ( from to --- c-addr u )
  2DUP = IF CASE-ERR THEN  OVER NSKIP 2DUP = IF CASE-ERR THEN  DUP NSKIP ROT <> IF CASE-ERR THEN   ( from blkw )
  DUP N+ DUP @ N-BK <> SWAP @A OR IF CASE-ERR THEN
  SWAP WORD-CODE T" D-TEXT" ++ TOP$  ROT N+ N+  0 >R
  BEGIN DUP @ WHILE  DUP >R N+  BEGIN DUP @ WHILE ARM-WORD  R> R> 1+ >R >R  REPEAT DROP  R> NSKIP  REPEAT DROP
  T" DROP 0 STATUS !" SEQ+  R> 0 ?DO T" THEN" SEQ+ LOOP ;
: IF-CMD ( from to --- c-addr u )
  2DUP TO-BLOCK 2DUP = IF S" if condition { ... } - a block, not sh's then and fi" G-ERR THEN
  ROT OVER FLAG T" IF" ++ 2 PICK INLINE ++  ROT NSKIP     \ else and elif see the condition's status, as sh's (902);
  DUP 4 PICK = IF DROP ROT DROP T" ELSE 0 STATUS ! THEN" ++ EXIT THEN    \ no branch taken: status 0
  DUP S" else" BARE= IF NSKIP DUP 4 PICK = IF ELSE-ERR THEN  DUP NSKIP 4 PICK <> IF ELSE-ERR THEN
    INLINE 2SWAP T" ELSE" ++ 2SWAP ++ T" THEN" ++ ROT DROP EXIT THEN
  DUP S" elif" BARE= IF NSKIP 3 PICK RECURSE 2SWAP T" ELSE" ++ 2SWAP ++ T" THEN" ++ ROT DROP EXIT THEN
  S" after if's block: else or elif" G-ERR ;
: LOOP-PLAIN? ( w --- f )   \ a loop's body with no break, no continue and no block in it: run plain (866)
  N+ DUP NSKIP SWAP N+
  BEGIN 2DUP <> WHILE
    DUP @ N-BK = IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN
    DUP @ N-WRD = IF DUP S" break" BARE= OVER S" continue" BARE= OR IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN THEN
  N+ REPEAT 2DROP -1 ;
: LOOP-BODY ( w c-addr u --- c-addr2 u2 id v )   \ a loop's body, a word of its own: its name, the slots of
  SCOPE(  S" %loop" 0 DECLARE V-SLOT >R            \ the loop's number and of its variable - fresh each time
  DUP IF 2DUP CAPTURED? DECLARE V-SLOT ELSE 2DROP 0 THEN >R
  S" L" FRESH  R@ SC @ CELL+ @ 5 CELLS + @ AND IF R@ T# T" LS@ UPV-NEW" ++ R@ T#++ T" LS!" ++ ELSE 0 0 THEN
  4 PICK N+ N+ BODY-CODE T" R-TURN" 2SWAP ++ ++  2OVER 2SWAP DEF-WORD  ROT LOOP-PLAIN?  R> R> SWAP  ROT IF NIP 0 SWAP THEN  )SCOPE ;   \ id 0: plain
: FOR-CMD ( from to --- c-addr u )   \ for name words... { body }
  OVER BARE? 0= 2 PICK NSKIP 2 PICK = OR IF S" for name words... { body }" G-ERR THEN
  OVER NSKIP S" in" BARE= IF S" for name values... { } - no in, as sh has" G-ERR THEN      \ it had gone round in too (916)
  FR @ F-SLOT >R  OVER SWAP LAST-W
  OVER NSKIP OVER ARGS-CODE
  3 PICK NSKIP DUP NSKIP 4 PICK = SWAP N+ @ N-SP <> AND IF T" FOR-ONE" ++ THEN
  R@ T#++ T" LS!" ++  R@ T#++
  2SWAP SWAP BARE$ LOOP-BODY
  OVER 0= IF NIP 4 ROLL 4 ROLL ROT T#++ 2SWAP T-TICK$ ++ T" C-FOR-PLAIN" ++ OK$ R> DROP EXIT THEN
  5 ROLL 5 ROLL ROT T#++ ROT T#++ 2SWAP T-TICK$ ++ T" C-FOR" ++ OK$  R> DROP ;
: WHILE-CMD ( from to --- c-addr u )   \ while condition { body }
  S" W" FRESH 2SWAP OVER SWAP LAST-W  TUCK FLAG ROT >R  2OVER 2SWAP DEF-WORD  R>
  0 0 LOOP-BODY DROP
  ?DUP 0= IF  >R >R T" BEGIN" 2SWAP ++ T" WHILE" ++ R> R> ++ T" REPEAT" ++ OK$ EXIT THEN   \ plain: compiled in place
  T#  5 ROLL 5 ROLL T-TICK$ ++  2SWAP T-TICK$ ++ T" C-WHILE" ++ OK$ ;
: NAME? ( c-addr u --- f )   \ a name: a letter or _ first; letters, digits, _, and - inside, not last (930: -, kebab-case)
  DUP 0= IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN  OVER C@ NAME0? 0= IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN  2DUP + 1- C@ [CHAR] - = IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  -1 ROT ROT 0 ?DO  DUP I + C@ DUP NAMEC? SWAP [CHAR] - = OR  ROT AND SWAP  LOOP DROP ;
: BIND ( from to --- name value )   \ var name value, set name value: their two words
  2DUP TWO? 0= IF S" var name value, set name value" G-ERR THEN  DROP DUP NSKIP ;
: IN-SCOPE? ( c-addr u --- f )   SC @ CELL+ @ VAR-IN 0<> ;   \ the name declared in this scope itself
: VALUE-CODE ( w --- c-addr u )   \ var's and set's value: a word's - or @( ) or @name's one value (896)
  DUP N+ @ N-SP = IF T" ARGL" ROT ARG-CODE ++ T" ONE" ++ EXIT THEN  WORD-CODE ;
: HOISTED ( c-addr u --- v | 0 )   \ the name known from the script's start, its var not yet met (929)
  SC @ CELL+ @ VAR-IN  DUP IF DUP 6 CELLS + @ -1 <> IF DROP 0 THEN THEN ;
VARIABLE FN-NEXT   \ the var being made has a block written as its value: a function (929)
: VAR-NEW ( c-addr u x --- slot captured? )   \ var's variable: its name checked, declared - x its 7th cell
  >R  2DUP NAME? 0= IF S" var: a name, not" S| 2SWAP ++ G-ERR THEN
  2DUP IN-SCOPE? SESSION @ 0= AND IF S| S" is declared here already - set changes it" ++ G-ERR THEN   \ (879)
  2DUP CAPTURED? DUP >R DECLARE  R> R> ROT TUCK 7 CELLS + !  V-SLOT SWAP ;
: VAR-FN ( nw vw --- c-addr u )   \ var f { ... } below the top level: f declared before its block is made, so
  SWAP BARE$                                      \ the block can call itself (930) - in its box, made first
  -1 VAR-NEW IF                                                                    ( vw slot )
    DUP >R T" 0 UPV-NEW" ROT T#++ T" LS!" ++  ROT VALUE-CODE ++  R> T#++ T" LS@ UPV!" ++ EXIT THEN
  >R VALUE-CODE R> T#++ T" LS!" ++ ;
: VAR-CMD ( from to --- c-addr u )   \ var name value
  BIND OVER BARE? 0= IF S" var: a name first" G-ERR THEN
  DUP N+ @ N-BK = IF OVER BARE$ 2DUP BUILTIN? IF   \ var run { }: run the builtin, the function never called by name (967)
    S| S" is a builtin's name - a function so named is never called by it; name it otherwise" ++ G-ERR THEN 2DROP THEN
  DUP N+ @ N-BK = IF OVER BARE$ HOISTED 0= IF VAR-FN EXIT THEN THEN
  DUP N+ @ N-BK = >R  VALUE-CODE ROT BARE$  R> FN-NEXT !
  2DUP HOISTED ?DUP IF NIP NIP 1 OVER 6 CELLS + !  V-SLOT T#++ T" LS!" ++ EXIT THEN   \ its slot, set now
  FN-NEXT @ VAR-NEW IF >R T" UPV-NEW" ++ R> THEN T#++ T" LS!" ++ ;
: SET-ERR ( --- )   S" a name to set" G-ERR ;
: GONE ( vr c-addr u c-addr2 u2 --- )   \ set name[k], read name[k], append, del (976): an element changes by its
  2SWAP S| S"  is gone (976) - $" CAT  4 PICK DUP @A SWAP @B CAT  2SWAP CAT G-ERR ;   \ value's operation - said so
: TARGET? ( w --- vr | 0 )   \ set's or read's: a name[key]..., a N-VR - or a plain name, a N-TX, where the reader
  N+ DUP @ N-VR = OVER NSKIP @ 0= AND IF EXIT THEN            \ took it as a word: while read line (886)
  DUP @ N-TX = OVER NSKIP @ 0= AND IF DUP @A OVER @B NAME? IF EXIT THEN THEN  DROP 0 ;
: TARGET ( w --- vr )   TARGET? ?DUP 0= IF SET-ERR THEN ;
: SET-TO ( vc vu vr --- c-addr u )   \ the value made by vc vu put in the target, a variable
  DUP @A SWAP @B  2DUP FIND-VAR ?DUP 0= IF S" no variable" S| 2SWAP ++ S" - var makes one, then set or read changes it" ++ G-ERR THEN
  NIP NIP  DUP 5 CELLS + @ IF REF ++ T" UPV!" ++ EXIT THEN
  DUP 3 CELLS + @ FR @ = IF V-SLOT T#++ T" LS!" ++ EXIT THEN
  DUP MAIN-V? IF V-SLOT T#++ T" MLS!" ++ EXIT THEN  S" cm: an unboxed variable set from a block" G-ERR ;
: GONE-OP ( from to c-addr u --- )   \ append, del as a first word (976): gone - where they went said
  2SWAP OVER <> IF  TARGET? ?DUP IF ROT ROT  2DUP S" append" COMPARE 0= IF S"  append values: a list's operation"
      ELSE S"  del key: a list's or a map's operation" THEN GONE THEN  ELSE DROP THEN
  S| S"  is gone (976) - $l append x, $m del k: operations" CAT G-ERR ;
: SET-CMD ( from to --- c-addr u )   \ set name value - its target read as $'s are (881); set name[k] v
  BIND SWAP TARGET  DUP N+ @ IF S" set name[key]" S"  set key value changes an element" GONE THEN   \ is $name set k v (976)
  >R VALUE-CODE R> SET-TO ;
: READ-CMD ( from to --- c-addr u )   \ read name: a line of stdin into it - status 1 at the end (886)
  OVER NSKIP <> IF  DUP BARE? IF DUP BARE$ S" -r" COMPARE 0= IF       \ read -r line, sh's habit (971): said so
      S" read takes one name - it reads a line as it is: no -r" G-ERR THEN THEN
    S" read takes one name" G-ERR THEN  TARGET  DUP N+ @ IF S" read name[key]" S"  set key $line, after read line" GONE THEN
  T" STDIN-LINE" ROT SET-TO ;
: WORDS# ( from to --- n )   0 ROT ROT BEGIN 2DUP <> WHILE SWAP NSKIP SWAP ROT 1+ ROT ROT REPEAT 2DROP ;
: PLAIN-ARGS0? ( from to x --- f )   DROP BEGIN 2DUP <> WHILE  OVER N+ @ N-SP = IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN  SWAP NSKIP SWAP  REPEAT 2DROP -1 ;   \ no spread
: STACK-CODE ( from to --- c-addr u )   \ each word's value, in order
  >R >R 0 0 TOP$  BEGIN R> R> 2DUP >R >R <> WHILE  R> DUP NSKIP >R WORD-CODE SEQ+ REPEAT  R> R> 2DROP ;
: CAP-IN? ( from to --- f )   \ a $( ) or @( ) among these words: var's and set's status theirs, as sh's x=$(cmd) (897)
  SWAP BEGIN 2DUP <> WHILE  DUP @ N-CP = IF 2DROP -1 EXIT THEN  N+ REPEAT 2DROP 0 ;
: METHOD? ( from to --- i | -1 )   \ $v op ...: the second word bare, an operation's name (967)
  SWAP NSKIP TUCK = IF DROP -1 EXIT THEN  DUP BARE? 0= IF DROP -1 EXIT THEN  BARE$ OP# ;
: METHOD-CODE ( from to i --- c-addr u )   \ ARGL, the value ARG, the words after op; op's number, CALL-METHOD
  >R >R  DUP NSKIP NSKIP >R  T" ARGL" ROT WORD-CODE ++ T" ARG" ++ TOP$
  BEGIN R> R@ OVER <> WHILE  DUP NSKIP >R ARG-CODE SEQ+ REPEAT  DROP R> DROP  R> T#++ T" CALL-METHOD" ++ ;
: ITEM-OP? ( from to i --- from to i f )   \ set k x, del k, append x, no spread among the words: code direct (976)
  DUP 11 14 WITHIN 0= IF 0 EXIT THEN
  >R 2DUP 0 PLAIN-ARGS0? 0= IF R> 0 EXIT THEN
  2DUP SWAP NSKIP NSKIP SWAP WORDS#  R@ 11 = 1 AND 1+ =  R> SWAP ;
: ITEM-CODE ( from to i --- c-addr u )   \ the value's code, its words', SET-ITEM APPEND-ITEM or DEL-ITEM
  >R  OVER WORD-CODE  2SWAP SWAP NSKIP NSKIP SWAP STACK-CODE ++
  R> DUP 11 = IF DROP T" SET-ITEM" ELSE 12 = IF T" APPEND-ITEM" ELSE T" DEL-ITEM" THEN THEN ++ ;
: SINGLE ( from to --- c-addr u )   \ one command, not a program's
  OVER N+ DUP @ N-BK = SWAP @B AND IF DROP INLINE EXIT THEN   \ a group, marked so (960)
  OVER BARE? 0= IF  2DUP METHOD? DUP 0< 0= IF ITEM-OP? IF ITEM-CODE ELSE METHOD-CODE THEN EXIT THEN DROP         \ rule 11: a value as the first word -
    OVER NSKIP OVER ARGS-CODE  ROT DROP ROT WORD-CODE ++ T" CALL-VALUE" ++ EXIT THEN   \ its operation, or it called
  OVER BARE$ 2SWAP SWAP NSKIP SWAP 2SWAP
  S" var" NAMED? IF 2DROP 2DUP CAP-IN? >R VAR-CMD R> 0= IF OK$ THEN EXIT THEN   \ status: its value's capture's (897)
  S" set" NAMED? IF 2DROP 2DUP CAP-IN? >R SET-CMD R> 0= IF OK$ THEN EXIT THEN
  S" read" NAMED? IF 2DROP READ-CMD EXIT THEN                   \ READ-LINE sets the status (886)
  S" put" NAMED? IF 2DROP  2DUP <> IF OVER NSKIP OVER = 2 PICK N+ @ N-SP <> AND IF DROP WORD-CODE T" PUT" ++ OK$ EXIT THEN THEN
    ARGS-CODE T" PUTS" ++ OK$ EXIT THEN                     \ put one value: PUT it, no list made (866)
  S" echo" NAMED? IF 2DROP  2DUP <> IF OVER S" -n" BARE= 2 PICK S" -e" BARE= OR IF   \ sh's echo options (932)
      S" echo -n and -e are sh's - echo prints its words and a newline; printf '%s' text prints none" G-ERR THEN THEN
    ARGS-CODE T" ECHO" ++ OK$ EXIT THEN
  2DUP S" cd exit wait trap forth" IN-LIST? IF >R >R ARGS-CODE R> R> UPPER S" -OF" CAT T-NAMED ++ EXIT THEN      \ they set the status themselves (873)
  2DUP S" range each kind glob" IN-LIST? IF >R >R ARGS-CODE R> R> UPPER S" -OF" CAT T-NAMED ++ OK$ EXIT THEN
  S" true" NAMED? IF 2DROP 2DROP T" 0 STATUS !" EXIT THEN
  S" false" NAMED? IF 2DROP 2DROP T" 1 STATUS !" EXIT THEN
  2DUP S" break continue" IN-LIST? IF 2SWAP 2DROP  S" %loop" FIND-VAR ?DUP 0= IF S" outside a loop" ++ G-ERR THEN
    REF 2SWAP UPPER T-NAMED ++ EXIT THEN
  S" return" NAMED? IF 2DROP 2DUP = IF 2DROP T" STATUS @" ELSE  OVER NSKIP <> IF S" return takes one status" G-ERR THEN
    WORD-CODE T" D>N" ++ THEN               \ (966: return 1 2 had been return 1; a bare return 0, where exit's is the last
                                            \ status, as sh's both)
    S" %def" FIND-VAR ?DUP 0= IF S" return outside a function - exit ends the script" G-ERR THEN   \ (968: it had
    REF ++ T" RETURN" ++ EXIT THEN                \ ended it at the top level - a sourced file's too - as exit)
  S" if" NAMED? IF 2DROP IF-CMD EXIT THEN
  S" case" NAMED? IF 2DROP CASE-CMD EXIT THEN                   \ its arm's status, or 0 (910)
  2DUP S" for while" IN-LIST? IF
    2OVER 2DUP = IF 2DROP 0 ELSE LAST-W N+ DUP @ N-BK = SWAP @A 0= AND THEN
    0= IF S" ... { body } - a block with no parameters" ++ G-ERR THEN
    S" for" COMPARE 0= IF FOR-CMD ELSE WHILE-CMD THEN EXIT THEN
  S" def" NAMED? IF S" def is gone (930) - var name {|params| ... } makes a function" G-ERR THEN
  S" source" NAMED? IF S" source is for the script's top level" G-ERR THEN    \ (890)
  2DUP FIND-FN IF  2SWAP 2DUP 999999 PLAIN-ARGS0? IF  2DUP WORDS# >R STACK-CODE R> T#++  2SWAP 2DUP >R >R READ$ ++  R> R> SQ$ ++  T" CALL-NAMED-S" ++ EXIT THEN
    ARGS-CODE  2SWAP 2DUP >R >R READ$ ++  R> R> SQ$ ++  T" CALL-NAMED" ++ EXIT THEN   \ a function (929): its arguments on the stack (930)
  S" append" NAMED? IF GONE-OP THEN  S" del" NAMED? IF GONE-OP THEN   \ (976: $l append x, $m del k)
  S" : no such command" CAT G-ERR ;

\ ---- pipelines (859, 862): programs side by side an OS pipeline, a function's stage run to its end
VARIABLE PL          \ the pipeline being made: [to][end][end's length][state: 0, 1 list, 2 path][code][its length][a segment's end][last?]
                     \ [a function's stage in it: PST's status (968)][its last segment programs']
: PL@ ( i --- x )   CELLS PL @ + @ ;
: PL! ( x i --- )   CELLS PL @ + ! ;
: PL+ ( c-addr u --- )   \ to the pipeline's code, joined in place as SEQ+ (891: a program given 5,000 words was too big)
  5 PL@ 0= IF TOP$ ELSE 4 PL@ 5 PL@ 2SWAP SEQ+ THEN 5 PL! 4 PL! ;
: RD-OP ( w --- c-addr u n )   \ a redirection's Forth after its file's, n 1 - a dup's, n 0 - or n -1, neither
  DUP BARE? 0= IF DROP 0 0 -1 EXIT THEN  BARE$
  S" >" NAMED? IF 2DROP T" W/O 1 RD-FILE" 1 EXIT THEN
  S" >>" NAMED? IF 2DROP T" A/O 1 RD-FILE" 1 EXIT THEN
  S" <" NAMED? IF 2DROP T" R/O 0 RD-FILE" 1 EXIT THEN
  S" <<" NAMED? IF 2DROP T" HD-FILE -2 0 RD-FILE" 1 EXIT THEN          \ its file read, then taken away (963)
  S" 2>" NAMED? IF 2DROP T" W/O 2 RD-FILE" 1 EXIT THEN
  S" 2>>" NAMED? IF 2DROP T" A/O 2 RD-FILE" 1 EXIT THEN
  S" &>" NAMED? IF 2DROP T" W/O 1 RD-FILE 1 2 R-RD-DUP" 1 EXIT THEN
  S" 2>&1" NAMED? IF 2DROP T" 1 2 R-RD-DUP" 0 EXIT THEN
  2DUP S" >&2 1>&2" IN-LIST? IF 2DROP T" 2 1 R-RD-DUP" 0 EXIT THEN
  2DROP 0 0 -1 ;
: RD-TARGET ( to w --- to w' c-addr u )   \ the file after a redirection: its word's code
  NSKIP DUP 2 PICK = IF S" a redirection wants a file" G-ERR THEN  DUP WORD-CODE ;
: STAGE-CODE ( from to last? --- )   \ a program's stage: its redirections, then its words - to the pipeline's code
  >R  2DUP SWAP
  BEGIN 2DUP <> WHILE
    DUP RD-OP DUP 0< IF DROP 2DROP NSKIP ELSE
      IF >R >R RD-TARGET PL+ R> R> PL+ NSKIP
      ELSE PL+ NSKIP THEN THEN
  REPEAT 2DROP
  T" ARGL" PL+  0 ROT ROT SWAP
  DUP S" run" BARE= IF NSKIP  2DUP = IF S" run takes a program's name, then its words" G-ERR THEN  THEN   \ (967)
  BEGIN 2DUP <> WHILE
    DUP RD-OP DUP 0< IF DROP 2DROP DUP ARG-CODE PL+ NSKIP ROT 1+ ROT ROT
    ELSE NIP NIP IF NSKIP THEN NSKIP THEN
  REPEAT 2DROP  0= IF S" a stage with no program" G-ERR THEN
  R> IF T" -1 PSTAGE" ELSE T" 0 PSTAGE" THEN PL+ ;
DEFER RD-SINGLE ( from to --- c-addr u )   \ one command, redirected or not: below
: SEG-END ( s --- e last? )   \ programs' segment's end: the | before a function's stage, or the pipeline's end
  BEGIN DUP 0 PL@ TO-PIPE DUP 0 PL@ = IF NIP -1 EXIT THEN  DUP NSKIP PROGRAM? 0= IF NIP 0 EXIT THEN  NSKIP NIP AGAIN ;
: PL-BG? ( --- f )   1 PL@ 2 PL@ S" &" COMPARE 0= ;     \ the pipeline ends in &: started, not waited for
: PST-FIRST ( --- )   \ the first segment, a function's stage after it - or one: PST's status, begun (968)
  5 PL@ 0= IF -1 8 PL!  T" PST(" PL+ THEN ;
: PROG-SEG ( cur --- cur' )
  DUP SEG-END 7 PL! 6 PL!  7 PL@ 0= IF PST-FIRST THEN
  PL-BG? IF T" 0 PL-BEGIN PL-NULL-IN" ELSE 7 PL@ 0= 2 PL@ OR IF T" 1 PL-BEGIN" ELSE T" 2 PL-BEGIN" THEN THEN PL+
  3 PL@ 2 = IF T" DUP R/O 0 RD-FILE" PL+ THEN
  BEGIN DUP 0 PL@ TO-PIPE TUCK DUP 6 PL@ = STAGE-CODE  DUP 6 PL@ <> WHILE NSKIP REPEAT DROP
  7 PL@ IF PL-BG? IF T" PL-SPAWN JOB !" ELSE 2 PL@ IF 1 PL@ 2 PL@ ELSE T" PIPE-END" THEN THEN ELSE T" PIPE-LINES" THEN
  2DUP PL+  T" PIPE-END" COMPARE  3 PL@ 2 = IF IF T" SWAP DEL-PATH" ELSE T" DEL-PATH" THEN PL+ ELSE DROP THEN
  8 PL@ IF T" PST+" PL+ THEN  7 PL@ 9 PL!
  7 PL@ 0= 1 AND 3 PL!  6 PL@ 7 PL@ 0= IF NSKIP THEN ;
: FN-SEG ( cur --- cur' )   \ a function's stage - its redirections run round it, as a lone command's (903)
  PST-FIRST  DUP 0 PL@ TO-PIPE DUP 6 PL!  S" S" FRESH 2SWAP SCOPE( RD-SINGLE )SCOPE 2OVER 2SWAP DEF-WORD
  3 PL@ IF 0 0 ELSE T" 0" THEN 2SWAP T-TICK$ ++          \ the first stage: no input, stdin as it is (882)
  6 PL@ 0 PL@ = IF T" FN-RUN" 0 ELSE 6 PL@ NSKIP PROGRAM? IF T" FN>FILE" 2 ELSE T" FN-LIST" 1 THEN THEN
  3 PL! ++ PL+  8 PL@ IF T" PST+" PL+ THEN  0 9 PL!  6 PL@ DUP 0 PL@ <> IF NSKIP THEN ;
: STAGES-OK ( from to --- )
  SWAP BEGIN 2DUP SWAP TO-PIPE TUCK = IF S" an empty stage in a pipeline" G-ERR THEN  2DUP <> WHILE NSKIP REPEAT 2DROP ;
: PIPELINE' ( from to c-addr u --- c-addr2 u2 )   \ c-addr u how it ends: 0 0 a run, its status; PIPE-TEXT, PIPE-LINES a capture
  2OVER STAGES-OK
  PL @ >R  10 RC PL !  2 PL! 1 PL! 0 PL!
  BEGIN DUP 0 PL@ <> WHILE DUP PROGRAM? IF PROG-SEG ELSE FN-SEG THEN REPEAT DROP
  8 PL@ IF  9 PL@ 2 PL@ 0<> AND IF T" )PST-V" ELSE T" )PST" THEN PL+  THEN
  4 PL@ 5 PL@  R> PL ! ;
' PIPELINE' IS PIPELINE
: ALL-PROGRAMS? ( from to --- f )   \ each stage's first word a program's
  SWAP BEGIN DUP PROGRAM? 0= IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN  2DUP SWAP TO-PIPE DUP 3 PICK = IF 2DROP DROP -1 EXIT THEN NIP NSKIP AGAIN ;
: BG? ( from to --- from to' f )   2DUP = IF 0 EXIT THEN  2DUP LAST-W DUP S" &" BARE= IF NIP -1 ELSE DROP 0 THEN ;
: RD-WORD? ( w --- f )   RD-OP NIP NIP 0< 0= ;
: TO-RD ( from to --- w )   SWAP BEGIN 2DUP <> WHILE DUP RD-WORD? IF NIP EXIT THEN NSKIP REPEAT DROP ;
VARIABLE RDA   VARIABLE RDU                       \ the redirections' Forth being made
: RD+ ( c-addr u --- )   RDA @ RDU @ 2SWAP ++ RDU ! RDA ! ;
: RD-CODE ( from to --- c-addr u )   \ a builtin's or a function's redirections, after its words (875)
  RDA @ >R RDU @ >R  0 RDA ! 0 RDU !  SWAP
  BEGIN 2DUP <> WHILE
    DUP RD-OP DUP 0< IF S" a builtin's or a function's redirections come after its words" G-ERR THEN
    IF >R >R RD-TARGET RD+ R> R> RD+ NSKIP
    ELSE RD+ NSKIP THEN
  REPEAT 2DROP  RDA @ RDU @  R> RDU ! R> RDA ! ;
: SEGMENT ( from to --- c-addr u )   \ a | b | c, or a program: a pipeline; else one command - ending in &: in the background
  OVER S" else" BARE= 2 PICK S" elif" BARE= OR IF S" else and elif follow an if's } - there is no if before this" G-ERR THEN   \ (877)
  BG? IF  2DUP = IF S" & after nothing" G-ERR THEN  2DUP ALL-PROGRAMS? 0= IF S" & runs programs - a function runs here" G-ERR THEN
    S" &" PIPELINE T" 0 STATUS !" ++ EXIT THEN                                        \ (874)
  2DUP TO-PIPE OVER <> 2 PICK PROGRAM? OR IF 0 0 PIPELINE EXIT THEN
  RD-SINGLE ;
: RD-SINGLE' ( from to --- c-addr u )   \ a builtin or a function, redirected (875): the command a word of its own,
  2DUP TO-RD DUP 2 PICK = IF DROP SINGLE EXIT THEN                      \ run by RD-RUN - alone, or a pipeline's stage
  DUP 3 PICK = IF S" a redirection with no command" G-ERR THEN
  TUCK SWAP RD-CODE 2SWAP  S" S" FRESH 2SWAP SCOPE( SINGLE )SCOPE 2OVER 2SWAP DEF-WORD
  2SWAP T" R-RD-RESET" 2SWAP ++ 2SWAP T-TICK$ ++ T" RD-RUN" ++ ;
' RD-SINGLE' IS RD-SINGLE
: ERR-ANDOR ( --- )   S" && and || stand between commands" G-ERR ;
: NEG-SEGMENT ( from to --- c-addr u )   \ ! cmd: its status turned, as sh's ! (914) - had run a program named !
  OVER S" !" BARE= IF  SWAP NSKIP SWAP  2DUP = IF S" ! wants a command" G-ERR THEN
    SEGMENT T" STATUS @ 0= 1 AND STATUS !" ++ EXIT THEN  SEGMENT ;
: SEG-CODE ( from to last? --- c-addr u )   \ a chain's command: checked if it is the last, tested if not
  >R OVER S" !" BARE= IF R> DROP NEG-SEGMENT T" TESTING+" 2SWAP ++ T" TESTING-" ++ EXIT THEN
  R> IF NEG-SEGMENT CHK @ IF T" STATUS @ IF ?FAIL THEN" ++ THEN ELSE NEG-SEGMENT T" TESTING+" 2SWAP ++ T" TESTING-" ++ THEN ;
: CMD-RANGE' ( from to --- c-addr u )   \ a && b || c, as sh chains them (859)
  TUCK OVER SWAP TO-ANDOR TUCK  2DUP = IF ERR-ANDOR THEN  3 PICK OVER = SEG-CODE
  BEGIN 3 PICK 3 PICK <> WHILE
    2 PICK S" &&" BARE= IF T" STATUS @ 0= IF" ELSE T" STATUS @ IF" THEN ++
    ROT NSKIP DUP 4 PICK TO-ANDOR 2DUP = IF ERR-ANDOR THEN  DUP >R DUP 5 PICK = SEG-CODE ++ T" THEN" ++ R> ROT ROT
  REPEAT  2SWAP 2DROP ;
' CMD-RANGE' IS CMD-RANGE

\ ---- a script
255 CONSTANT SESSION-SLOTS
: NAMES-NEW ( --- )   \ no names yet: a script's, or a session's start
  0 CAPS !  0 CAPS-CAP !
  0 NEW-FRAME FR !  0 SC !  SCOPE(  S" %main" 0 0 VAR+ DROP  FR @ MAIN-FR !  SC @ MAIN-SC ! ;   \ slot 0: no %def, no return
: SCRIPT$ ( --- c-addr u )   SESSION @ SYS-ARGC 1 < OR IF S" " ELSE 0 SYS-ARG DUP CSTRLEN THEN ;
: SF-START ( c-addr u --- )   \ the script's, or a prompt line's: texts freed - their words are made; a script's files
  \ forgotten, names too; at the prompt those of earlier lines kept, their line ranges past 2^20, never a line's own
  SF-T @ 0= IF  8 DUP SF-CAP !  DUP 6 * CELLS ALLOCATE THROW SF-T !  5 * CELLS ALLOCATE THROW SF-S !  THEN
  SF-N @ 1 MAX 1 ?DO  I SF 4 CELLS + DUP @ ?DUP IF FREE DROP THEN  0 SWAP !  LOOP
  SESSION @ IF  SF-BASE @ 1 MAX  ELSE 1 THEN  >R                 \ from here on, made again
  SF-N @ 1 MAX R@ MAX R@ ?DO  I SF 2 CELLS + @ FREE DROP  LOOP  R@ SF-N !
  SESSION @ IF R> ELSE R> DROP 0 THEN SF-LINE0 !
  0 SF-SP !  0 SF-CUR !  0 SF-SEEN !  0 TOP-CMD !
  LINES#  SESSION @ IF SF-NEXT @ 1 20 LSHIFT MAX SF-NEXT ! ELSE DUP SF-NEXT ! THEN
  0 SF CELL+ !  0 0 SF !  SCRIPT$ 0 SF 3 CELLS + !  0 SF 2 CELLS + !  0 0 SF 5 CELLS + ! ;
: HOIST ( cmd --- )   \ var name ... at the top level: the name declared now, unboxed, known from the start (929)
  N+ DUP S" var" BARE= 0= IF DROP EXIT THEN  NSKIP DUP @ 0= IF DROP EXIT THEN  DUP BARE? 0= IF DROP EXIT THEN
  DUP BARE$ 2DUP NAME? 0= IF 2DROP DROP EXIT THEN  2DUP IN-SCOPE? IF 2DROP DROP EXIT THEN        ( w c u )
  0 DECLARE -1 OVER 6 CELLS + !  SWAP NSKIP DUP @ IF N+ @ N-BK = ELSE DROP 0 THEN SWAP 7 CELLS + ! ;
: CM-COMPILE1 ( c-addr u --- c-addr2 u2 )   \ a script's text made Forth - the output, to EVALUATE
  DUP IN-LEN ! OVER IN-TEXT ! 0 IN-POS ! 1 IN-LINE ! -1 HD-AT ! 0 IN-HD !  2DUP SF-START  NIP SF-MORE @ +
  DUP 6 * 64 + 3 * CELLS ND0 NDP NDE AREA   DUP 2* 64 + TX0 TXP TXE AREA
  DUP 64 * 65536 + CH0 CHP CHE AREA   DUP 64 * 65536 + OU0 OUP OUE AREA
  SESSION @ RH0 @ 0<> AND IF DROP ELSE  16 * 4096 + CELLS  1 20 LSHIFT SESSION @ AND MAX  RH0 RHP RHE AREA  NAMES-NEW  THEN
  MAIN-FR @ FR !  MAIN-SC @ SC !  0 PL !  0 AP !     \ a session's line after an error: back at the top
  ND0 @  0 GROUP-W !  0 0 CMDS N)  GEN0
  SCAN-CAPS
  SESSION @ 0= IF DUP BEGIN DUP @ WHILE  DUP HOIST  NSKIP REPEAT DROP THEN   \ (929) - the prompt's lines are compiled one by one
  0 0 TOP$ ROT BEGIN DUP @ WHILE  DUP >R CMD-CODE DUP IF T" R-GC?" 2SWAP ++ THEN SEQ+  R> NSKIP REPEAT DROP
  SESSION @ IF
    S" M" FRESH 2SWAP 2OVER 2SWAP T-DEF 2SWAP ++ OUT+     \ run in the session's frame - made, then run
